, you da bes.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>And of course many thanks to Mr. Gone for the original template files.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! Those are pretty cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And you're very welcome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T13:54:06-07:00","id":552113,"title":"","content":"For those who care I updated my Mummy 2E doc with Utterances from Guildhalls of the Deathless. As with the core Utterances it was largely a case of pulling out all the stops and improving power and duration.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#heading=h.ue5thxct1jwo\" target=\"_blank\">Read 'em here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T01:00:45-07:00","id":634343,"title":"","content":"Hello, are you planning to look at Flowers of Hell for reviewing Embeds and Exploits? I really like what you did with the core book and since my group is starting a Demon campaing I wondered if you're planning it, or if I should see what I can do myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T23:18:22-07:00","id":636721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=634343#post634343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, are you planning to look at Flowers of Hell for reviewing Embeds and Exploits? I really like what you did with the core book and since my group is starting a Demon campaing I wondered if you're planning it, or if I should see what I can do myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was not my intention to mark up Flowers of Hell in the same way I did Demon: The Decent. Indeed, it was only possible to present demon as I did because the beta text was (and still is) available in full online.<br /> <br /> However, as you are not the first person to request this I may reconsider, and take some time away from updating Half-Awake to 2e to look over and provide notes for Flowers of Hell. That said, the notes would likely be considerably less thorough than those for the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T06:45:04-07:00","id":636936,"title":"","content":"Notes would be more than sufficient <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I did consider the fact that Demon: The Descent is available, while Flowers are not, so with just the notes, we could make our own document for our own use <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> I did make such a document already, doing some changing (mostly resistances). And the only one which really jump to my eyes as &quot;is this really Embed power lvl?&quot; was Imagine. <br /> So if you can't provide your own notes on more stuff, could you at least provide your opinion on Imagine? <br /> (full notes would be appreciated as well )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T17:34:19-08:00","id":780812,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I made a thing:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You Do Not Have To Bow</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Core Power: Imbuing Mortals</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keys</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Stigmata Marionette</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Power + Occult</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Indefinite</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dealing one lethal damage to himself by I made a thing: drawing blood with a dagger, he makes a mark of blood upon a mortal\u2019s brow. This mark is an \u201cobject\u201d with a Size of 1 and a Durability of (Successes), if this mark is destroyed by damage of any sort the Manifestation will end. Otherwise it cannot be removed, except for the Sin-Eater willing it. A mortal marked with this Manifestation gains the ability to touch and see ghosts, as well as Sin-Eater Damage Resistance by spending Willpower instead of Plasm. This Manifestation may not be used on more mortals than (Psyche) at a time. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Link #1: Night Falls...</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keys</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Primeval Caul</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trigger</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: &quot;When an imbued mortal faces a ghost in battle...&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">...he takes a point of lethal damage, automatically Goes for Blood and does not lose Defense from multiple opponents. He grows long, slender claws and fangs to replace frail fingers that do +0L, but each turn he </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>must</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> roll Resolve + Composure - (The number of rounds the battle has gone on), a failure means that he cannot target anything but the ghost and will attempt to devour the ghost when he has brought it to below half of it\u2019s Corpus. Failure to devour the ghost causes him to lose a point of Willpower and the transformation lasts for a scene.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Link #2: ...But The Sun Also Rises</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keys</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Stigmatic Pit</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trigger</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: \u201cWhen an imbued mortal devours a ghost\u2026\u201d</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">...the mark on his brow shines brightly and the ghost dissolves to lay over the mortal, granting him access to one if it\u2019s Numina which uses a dice pool of (lowest Power Attribute) + (lowest Finesse Attribute). This Numen lasts for a week, unless the mortal willingly spends a Willpower </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>dot</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, in which case he gains access to the Numen permanently. He uses the Numen by spending Willpower.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T13:42:04-08:00","id":782474,"title":"","content":"Hot damn, didn't think anyone even looked at that doc anymore.<br /> <br /> What the hell, I'll add these to the list (with a bit of tweaking, if you don't mind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T11:50:26-08:00","id":784878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=782474#post782474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hot damn, didn't think anyone even looked at that doc anymore.<br /> <br /> What the hell, I'll add these to the list (with a bit of tweaking, if you don't mind).</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, I'd love to see your changes to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T14:22:23-08:00","id":835372,"title":"","content":"For any interested I've made considerable changes to my Vampire, Werewolf and Demon Hacks. As well as added a Beta of Mage 2e House Rules based on DaveB's wonderful spoilers. Summary of changes below:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><u><b>Vampire</b></u></a><ul><li>Dropped Clans entirely in favor of Bloodlines, and adapted all five clans, and 12 additional bloodlines to 2e.</li> <li>Refocused Vampire society to include a lot more Revenants.</li> <li>Made changes to Siring to reflect the above two changes.</li> </ul><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><u><b>Werewolf</b></u></a><ul><li>Dropped Global Tribes in favor of local packs and lodges.</li> <li>Made it possible to shift Auspice as a Werewolf's place in their pack changes.</li> <li>Dropped the Pure entirely. They are too cartoon evil for my tastes.</li> </ul><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><u><b>Mage</b></u></a><ul><li>In addition to the changes in 2e, I de-emphasized paths, dropped the Exarchs, and lots of other things.</li> <li>Please keep in mind that the doc is a work in progress.</li> </ul><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><u><b>Demon</b></u></a><ul><li>Made changes to facilitate easier crossover without God-Machine involvement.</li> <li>Glitches are now the primary risk of Cover breach, and Demons are freer to act as invasive weirdos in the games of other lines.</li> </ul>As always constructive feedback is appreciated. Though I'd appreciate if comments like &quot;I like the original better&quot; be left out of the conversation (seriously, it's a homebrew thread, if you don't like a change ignore it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 02-22-2016, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T16:41:41-08:00","id":835457,"title":"","content":"I like your changes to Demon. My suggestions:<ul><li>In addition to the Major Brand or Tell, each Stigmatic has a way of generating Aether as part of the template, similarly to the Potent Blood Merit (Flowers Of Hell page 130). However, the method varies a lot, and isn't limited to hurtful secretions, but it is always detrimental in some way. For example, they might temporarily or permanently remove Attribute and Skill dots like a Mage Scouring their own Pattern, or inflict Conditions and Tilts on themselves at will. The amount of Aether is proportional to the loss, but no Stigmatic can generate more than 5 Aether per chapter. Wise Demons do not abuse their Stigmatic allies, and offer rewards for services rendered.</li> <li>Greater use of Cryptids as spying and Aether-hunting tools. All Cryptids now have the Aether Hive Adaptation. Should they have the [Fuelstat] Eater Adaptation, they convert it into Aether. They still need to spend this resource to remain alive, but many are willing to share in exchange for protection or anything else their strange minds can desire.</li> <li>Demons can dismantle Gadgets to absorb the Aether stored inside, but they cannot learn the installed Embed, Exploit or Demonic Form advantage if they do this. They must touch the Gadget, spend 1 willpower point and roll Wits + Science or Occult + Primum as an instant action. They gain 1 Aether automatically, in addition to Successes. This requires a Compromise roll, following Pendragon's house rules (or pings Aetheric Resonance, if you still want to use that in this situation). The Gadget cannot be a One-Shot or temporary, and if a Demon dismantles a Gadget they created, the Willpower <u>dot</u> is not returned.</li> <li>Allow the Essence Drain Technology to work on all supernaturals, and change its name to just Energy Drain. Ephemeral beings use their [Resistance/2 round up] as their Resolve to Resist the Demon's Wits + Occult + Primum roll.</li> <li>The Extispicy Exploit can now be used to absorb Aether, like a mortal being sacrificed to turn their Integrity into Essence for an Angel. The Aether gained is equal to Successes, capped by the mortal's [Integrity/2 round up]. Exploits that already absorbed Aether, such as Devour Infrastructure, may still do that, and other Exploits may absorb Aether as an alternate effect at the ST's discretion.</li> </ul>How does that sound, Pendragon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-22-2016, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T16:53:38-08:00","id":835462,"title":"","content":"Wooo, quite a list, and some great ideas. Let me parse them one-by-one.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=835457#post835457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]In addition to the Major Brand or Tell, each Stigmatic has a way of generating Aether as part of the template, similarly to the Potent Blood Merit (Flowers Of Hell page 130). However, the method varies a lot, and isn't limited to hurtful secretions, but it is always detrimental in some way. For example, they might temporarily or permanently remove Attribute and Skill dots like a Mage Scouring their own Pattern, or inflict Conditions and Tilts on themselves at will. The amount of Aether is proportional to the loss, but no Stigmatic can generate more than 5 Aether per chapter. Wise Demons do not abuse their Stigmatic allies, and offer rewards for services rendered.[*]Greater use of Cryptids as spying and Aether-hunting tools. All Cryptids now have the Aether Hive Adaptation. Should they have the [Fuelstat] Eater Adaptation, they convert it into Aether. They still need to spend this resource to remain alive, but many are willing to share in exchange for protection or anything else their strange minds can desire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll pass on these. Part of the aim with Stigmatics and Cryptids (and I can say this confidently, I wrote them) was to hit the infinite and alien aspects of the God-Machine head on. Cryptids can be literally anything, one can never assume with a Cryptid. Stigmatics less so, but they are still wildly varied. That said, I will add a note about using them for this purpose if you (the storyteller) are looking for other G-M related avenues to Aether.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=835457#post835457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Demons can dismantle Gadgets to absorb the Aether stored inside, but they cannot learn the installed Embed, Exploit or Demonic Form advantage if they do this. They must touch the Gadget, spend 1 willpower point and roll Wits + Science or Occult + Primum as an instant action. They gain 1 Aether automatically, in addition to Successes. This requires a Compromise roll, following Pendragon's house rules (or Aetheric Resonance, if you still want to use that in this situation). If a Demon dismantles a Gadget they created, the Willpower <u>dot</u> is not returned.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good idea. I'll add this (wrote Aetheric Resonane as well, so that'll see use).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=835457#post835457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Allow the Essence Drain Technology to work on all supernaturals, and change its name to just Energy Drain. Ephemeral beings use their [Resistance/2 round up] as their Resolve to Resist the Demon's Wits + Occult + Primum roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'll do a variant of this. Energy Drain takes Essence first, beings without Essence merely get shredded as the Demon unravels them for Aether.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=835457#post835457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]The Extispicy Exploit can now be used to absorb Aether, like a mortal being sacrificed to turn their Integrity into Essence for an Angel. The Aether gained is equal to Successes, capped by the mortal's [Integrity/2 round up]. Exploits that already absorbed Aether, such as Devour Infrastructure, may still do that, and other Exploits may absorb Aether as an alternate effect at the ST's discretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not gonna change Extispicy, but might write a new Exploit. <br /> <br /> This is all good feedback, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T17:37:16-08:00","id":835478,"title":"","content":"I'm glad I could help.<br /> <br /> Another idea I just had was to create a Merit that lets Demons temporarily downgrade but not remove Glitches, since they'll have a lot more of those under your house rules. Let me try. I chose that name because Glitches are also known as Bugs and I couldn't resist that pun. Change the name if you want, no problem. Do you think this makes Glitches trivial? Should I add more prerequisites?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Bug Spray</b></u> (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Intelligence 3, Composure 3, Occult 3<br /> <br /> <b>Effects: </b>Spend Aether equal to the number of Glitches you want to downgrade + 1 willpower point and roll Intelligence + Composure.as an instant action. The Aether expenditure is capped by your dots in this Merit. On a Success, they are downgraded one step for the scene (Catastrophic -&gt; Major -&gt; Minor). On an Exceptional Success, they are downgraded two steps. You may also sacrifice a willpower dot to make it last the whole chapter, but you can only do this once per story. You may decrease your effective Primum for the rest of the chapter to lower the threshold of an Exceptional Success. For each dot removed, one less Success is required, down to a minimum of one. Your Attributes, Skills, Fuelstat, Demonic Form advantages and Merits with a Primum prerequisite are lowered or removed accordingly. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T17:50:14-08:00","id":835482,"title":"","content":"Okay, I legit laughed out loud when I read the name of that merit.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'll use a merit, mostly because, as you said, it will probably be so important that all Demons will want it. But you've given me a fair idea for an approach: Deep Cover. Basically locking yourself into your cover to temporarily boost it's efficacy, with the kicker that if you break cover what-so-ever it is instant compromise.<br /> <br /> Bug Spray makes a fucking great gadget though. So I might include it as that, the name alone warrants it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T18:00:58-08:00","id":835484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=835482#post835482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I legit laughed out loud when I read the name of that merit.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'll use a merit, mostly because, as you said, it will probably be so important that all Demons will want it. But you've given me a fair idea for an approach: Deep Cover. Basically locking yourself into your cover to temporarily boost it's efficacy, with the kicker that if you break cover what-so-ever it is instant compromise.<br /> <br /> Bug Spray makes a fucking great gadget though. So I might include it as that, the name alone warrants it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Giving silly names to impressive things is always good for a laugh. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Please tell me when you've got a draft of Cover Hardening. I assume you won't be able to change Covers, enter complete or partial Demonic Form, spam Embeds, use the Monkeywrencher Merit and so on. I'd prefer it if you could still spend willpower points to cancel the compromise roll required by Exploits. I would also appreciate the option of spending willpower points to cancel the compromise roll required by assuming partial Demonic Form. I'd say one willpower point per advantage manifested, disregarding normal limits for willpower expenditure, and you still have to spend Aether. You can't do that when you assume complete Demonic Form, so no healing and no Aether restoration. Good luck if you run out of willpower points. By instant compromise, I assume you mean an automatic decrease of Cover, denying the usual Wits + Manipulation roll.<br /> <br /> Would Bug Spray be a Lambda? Going Native + Interference + Reality Reinforcement, maybe?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I see you renamed Cover Hardening to Deep Cover, but the latter is already the name of a Mundane Embed. I would name it Low Profile, in contrast to Going Loud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-22-2016, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T18:19:29-08:00","id":836133,"title":"","content":"Weird. I could have sworn you typed Cover Hardening before renaming it to Deep Cover. The latter is a Mundane Embed, so I'd call the mechanic Low Profile.<br /> <br /> Thank you for adding my suggestions to the GoogleDoc.<br /> <br /> By the way, you said that harvesting Aether from magic items suffers a penalty, but you listed the penalty for Lambdas as a bonus. I'd be better if you made it explicit that Essence Drain is a Technology. Also, I'm pretty sure Resistant damage cannot be healed with magic, rather than only with magic. You have to wait or use the Medicine Skill mundanely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-23-2016, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T19:42:09-08:00","id":836171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=836133#post836133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird. I could have sworn you typed Cover Hardening before renaming it to Deep Cover. The latter is a Mundane Embed, so I'd call the mechanic Low Profile.<br /> <br /> Thank you for adding my suggestions to the GoogleDoc.<br /> <br /> By the way, you said that harvesting Aether from magic items suffers a penalty, but you listed the penalty for Lambdas as a bonus. I'd be better if you made it explicit that Essence Drain is a Technology. Also, I'm pretty sure Resistant damage cannot be healed with magic, rather than only with magic. You have to wait or use the Medicine Skill mundanely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, thanks for all the feedback. I fell way under the weather today, hence the slow response.<br /> <br /> Changed the Aether mistype, renamed Deep Cover to Low Profile, and tweaked the damage wording. Now to get that Lambda Gadget in there, and I suppose any other Gadgets that come to mind over time. Going Native + Reality Enforcement + Interference seems pretty much perfect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T08:27:45-08:00","id":837569,"title":"","content":"I got board. Here's two new Arts for you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Haberdashery</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Why is a hat the most common symbol of authority? A crown, a mitre, a feathered headdress. On every continent headgear is a potent symbol of authority, belonging, or expertise. The prime Yantra for all Haberdashers. The Silver Ladder believe that somewhere in the Supernal the symbol of authority adorns his head and all Earthly authority follows; but despite their claims the Ladder did not invent Haberdashery. The Art arose independently from many mundane hatmaking guilds and trade associates around the world. Many of these were absorbed whole by the Ladder; the rest are dismissive referred to as mere hedge magicians for their lack of occult philosophy and general focus on using magic for purely mundane ends. Though the Ladder is always welcoming if a Haberdasher decides that magic is more interesting than winning the New York Fashion show.<br /> <br /> The term Milliner or Millinery is occasionally used for female Haberdasher, any Haberdasher spell using a women's hat, or a Haberdasher currently using a feminine occult role, or the term is not used at all. It depends where in the world you are.<br /> <br /> Resonant Path: Oribamus<br /> <br /> Primary Arcana: Prime, along with Mind<br /> <br /> Yantra: Making a hat by hand is the only possible Yantra available to Haberdashers. It is not a particularly potent Art.<br /> <br /> Rotes: Haberdasher rotes can do one of two things. Either they can cast an effect upon the wearer, or they can cast a Mind effect upon everyone who sees the wearer. A builder's hard hat could bestow Skill in construction or convince everyone on the building site that the Haberdasher is on the construction team. Within this limit any effect that's symbolically appropriate for the chosen hat is possible, the hard hat could also grant mage armour, convince anyone the Haberdasher talks too that they're currently employing builders, or physically transform the Haberdasher into someone who looks like a builder.<br /> <br /> Attainments<br /> <br /> Hat Making: Haberdashery is not a particularly potent art, but what they do they do well. A Haberdasher must make a hat to cast a spell, the effect begins when the hat is first worn and the hat falls apart at the end. In addition even the most novice Haberdasher can make Imbued Items and add their Crafts skill to all Imbuing rolls. Naturally they can only imbue headgear.<br /> <br /> Pointy Hat: When the Haberdashers say that headgear is a nearly universal icon, they're not kidding. Even wizards are in on the act. Haberdashers can create Grimoires in the form of any hat associated with Mages, and they can do so in partnership with another Mage who actually knows the desired Rotes. The more thematically appropriate the hat is for the spells within the better. Anyone wearing the hat gains the full benefits, which has the advantage of leaving the wearers hand's free for casting. The Grimoire may be Imbued with other effects.<br /> <br /> Hats for Kings: A Mind effect to convince everyone you're the role implied by your headgear is a popular Haberdashery effect. At this level it becomes an Attainment and can be done with any hat rather than just those hand made by Haberdashers for the purpose.<br /> <br /> Crowns for commoners: The interesting thing about hats, is that a top hat is just a potent symbol of the Victorian Era as Queen Victoria's crown. Hat's are as much about belonging as they are about authority or expertise. Belonging to a time, a place, a society. By donning an ordinary hat popular with the general public, the Haberdasher becomes temporally mortal. No magic short of Archmastery can detect their supernatural nature, all sympathetic links to their Shadow Name fail, and any Supernal magic or attainments currently affecting them are suspended. Haberdashers use this to hide from both the Abyss and the God Machine, as well as magical rivals, but if cornered they can regain their magic as easily as removing their hat.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Dumbledore's Army</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> If the Supernal is a reflection of humanity, does it not stand to reason that humanity suddenly falling in love with a story of magic and wonder would cast a bright reflection upon the Supernal? Dumbledore's Army insist that it does, and this art was not discovered by occult experimentation but intentionally created by Traditionalists who were sure it must exist just waiting for practitioners.<br /> <br /> They were right, and Dumbledore's Army has become a popular art due to it's flexibility and it's self affirming philosophies, and has been attracting an unusual number of young Mage's who's mystery play leads them to the DA's door. They've even built a school to attract them, currently it's small enough that the head (and only) teacher is the Astral Walker of Albus Dumbledoor himself.<br /> <br /> <br /> Resonant Path: Oribamus<br /> <br /> Primary Arcana: Forces, though DA is spread almost evenly among all Arcana, with a noticeable weakness in Fate, Spirit, and Death.<br /> <br /> Yantra: Wands, potions, pseudo-Latin incarnations, odd devices, robes, school uniforms, textbooks, the British school system, symbolically adopting occult roles based on Harry Potter characters. The Art's most potent Yantra is a Harry, a Ron and a Hermione acting in concert.<br /> <br /> Rotes: Due to the poorly defined rules and logic underlying magic in Harry Potter Dumbledore's Army are capable of almost every effect and have easy access to Yantras; however they have trouble building up truly impressive Reaches or large dicepools. Their rotes tend to be quick, easy, and produce relatively small effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> Attainments<br /> <br /> The Wand Choose The Wizard: Dumbledore's Army gain a Wand as a dedicated focus tool for free. A mentor does something simple like buy a set of cheap Harry Potter merchandise wands and asks his apprentice to choose the one which feels right. Inevitably it will turn out to be an authentic occult item made from wood and supernal regents. Members of the DA must use a Wand as a Yantra in every spell they cast, though some radicals use a staff. Using or creating imbued items is an exception.<br /> <br /> Sorting Hat: The philosophical core of DA is that your choices define you more than accidents of birth or Awakening; and that this in turn puts the responsibility on you to choose Griffindore not Slytherin (Mages being Mages, most are in fact Ravenclaw). A Mage in with this Attainment gains the Virtuous Merit for free and chooses the Virtue; in addition if they fulfil their new Virtue they gain +2 to the next Degeneration check they make this Session.<br /> <br /> Choosing a Slytherin like Virtue such as Ambition would be heavily frowned upon by the Art, though choosing one unconnected to the philosophy of Harry Potter would be even worse. This philosophy also means DA tend to strongly identify with their Shadow persona over their mundane one \u2013 though it is easier to ask your Mortal parents to call you Hermione than Thoth.<br /> <br /> Letter by Owl: Members of Dumbledore's Army may temporarily take a Sleeper outside of normalcy. The Sleeper's contacts consider it perfectly normal that their friend or family member will go away for a while (unless they roll well to resist of course), and the Sleeper themself becomes a Sleepwalker for the duration. The effect cannot last longer than one school term, as defined by the British government and can never be used on the same person twice.<br /> <br /> Inspiring a Generation: At their apex a member of DA treats any place where a large group of Sleepers are focusing on the Harry Potter stories or related merchandise as a Demanse.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> BTW a could of suggestions. I think twinspinners should use voodoo dolls rather than reflections as an Atainment. The charachter who inspired the art had a lot of voodoo trappings. Bezalel Kabbalism really should use Hebrew rather than Atlantian Runes - and it's practitioners should believe that Hebrew is a higher language than Atlantian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T10:30:41-08:00","id":837654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=837569#post837569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got board. Here's two new Arts for you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Goodie goodie.<br /> <br /> These are cool, though too narrow in scope and a tad lighthearted for my taste. However I think I can add variants that keep these concepts playable, while also expanding the arts to slightly different interpretations. Currently what I'm thinking is:<ul><li>An art of style and fashion, employing clothing, makeup and body image to touch on the zeitgeist and manipulate the world symbolically. Haberdashery will likely be noted as an origin, and populate for it's simplicity and easy of taking on and off.</li> <li>An art of fiction buffs, who use the styles of magic from television and literature to tap the growing symbols therein. Mages will be noted as picking 'favorite' works, and tending to focus on those. So a Harry Potter buff would use magic as you've presented it, while someone enamored with Lord of the Rings would go the Gandalf approach.</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=837569#post837569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW a could of suggestions. I think twinspinners should use voodoo dolls rather than reflections as an Atainment. The charachter who inspired the art had a lot of voodoo trappings. Bezalel Kabbalism really should use Hebrew rather than Atlantian Runes - and it's practitioners should believe that Hebrew is a higher language than Atlantian.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Twinspinners: </b>I was thinking of going broader on that yes. Not just voodoo dolls, but any realistic depiction. Photos, paintings, sculpture.<br /> <br /> <b>Atlantean Runes: </b>I'll make this clearer in the doc, but Atlantean Runes isn't a particular set of letters. They are more or less a way of inscribing magic, in fact I'll drop the word Atlantean altogether. Point is, Bezalel would absolutely use Hebrew symbols as their runes (though they would proudly explain it is the arithmetic hidden within the words that has the power). Actually, that gives me an idea for a merit...<br /> <br /> Thanks for all the feedback TKR, it's great even if I don't use it verbatim. I'll make sure you get proper attribution for Pyre Witchcraft and Twinspinning as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 02-26-2016, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T11:11:51-08:00","id":837676,"title":"","content":"Oh, Pyre Witchcraft isn't my idea. Someone suggested it to me as a possible Geist antagonist when I was trying a Geist revised. I forgot who though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T13:05:05-08:00","id":837728,"title":"","content":"Something occurred to me. How do Glitches under the new Demon house rules interact with Restoration Facilities (pages 186 and 187 of the Core)? I assume this type of Infrastructure would increase Cover to downgrade the associated Glitches, similar to Low Profile. Am I right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T13:48:24-08:00","id":837748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=837728#post837728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something occurred to me. How do Glitches under the new Demon house rules interact with Restoration Facilities (pages 186 and 187 of the Core)? I assume this type of Infrastructure would increase Cover to downgrade the associated Glitches, similar to Low Profile. Am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. That sounds about right.<br /> <br /> Honestly I hadn't given it a whole lot of thought, given that the hacks were primarily to use Demons as presented in Descent, but without heavy G-M presence. It deserves a note though, I think I'll follow your advice and make such Infrastructure capable of restoring Cover Dots directly, but make it clear that that sort of shit is how you get the G-M directly involved in a game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T17:17:57-08:00","id":837817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=837748#post837748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. That sounds about right.<br /> <br /> Honestly I hadn't given it a whole lot of thought, given that the hacks were primarily to use Demons as presented in Descent, but without heavy G-M presence. It deserves a note though, I think I'll follow your advice and make such Infrastructure capable of restoring Cover Dots directly, but make it clear that that sort of shit is how you get the G-M directly involved in a game.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're an Inquisitor, dammit! Giving a whole lot of thought about stuff is your <b>job</b>. <i><b>&gt;=[</b></i><br /> <br /> Thanks for using my feedback again.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T17:39:43-08:00","id":837826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=837817#post837817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're an Inquisitor, dammit! Giving a whole lot of thought about stuff is your <b>job</b>. <i><b>&gt;=[</b></i><br /> <br /> Thanks for using my feedback again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cross thread callback, very nice.<br /> <br /> I'll scold the tiny shadow people for their oversight.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T16:25:01-08:00","id":838262,"title":"","content":"I gave the new Mage 2ED house rules a read. Awesome! I always like homebrew that allows for more versatile character creation. I didn't like the Seers and Exarchs, so it's nice seeing them replaced with Prelacies. I am tempted to write an Art themed after the Supernal Symbol of the Hero, from Heracles to Superman and everything in between. Their Attainments would include the capacity to treat Sleeper witnesses to obvious magic as Sleepwalkers, if the magic is being used in accordance to a heroic persona. I got that idea from the section in the Mage Chronicler's Guide about making Superhero Mages. Their Yantras would include their hero costumes (which might be normal clothes if they want), certain rules of conduct (which can be anti-heroic) and so on. I just don't know if I should go for semi-serious or full Comic Book Silver Age shenanigans.<br /> <br /> By the way, I caught an error: you said Arts replaced Legacies, but you still mentioned the latter in the fifth dot of the Masque Merit.<br /> <br /> EDIT: What sort of Art do you think Acanthus!Doctor would focus on? The Quantum Men have some fitting Attainments, but their link to the God-Machine doesn't jive with him. He'd be a Free Councilor, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-27-2016, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T16:41:13-08:00","id":838271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=838262#post838262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gave the new Mage 2ED house rules a read. Awesome! I always like homebrew that allows for more versatile character creation. I didn't like the Seers and Exarchs, so it's nice seeing them replaced with Prelacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I've sunk an inordinate amount of time into it, so I'm glad to be told it doesn't suck :P<br /> <br /> It should also be noted that these Mage hacks are actually fairly well tested. I've run Mages, both PCs and NPCs, using them and they've turned out pretty great. More groundwork during character creation to get Arts, Rotes and Attainments hammered out, but the end result is quite rewarding. For instance I ran an Awakened Proximi game which contained two Acanthus, both with Fate 4 and Time 3, but you'd never have know their sheets were so similar if you just read a recount. The one themed all his magic with oaths and promises, taking a very fairytale feel, while the other used ghosts, anchors and karma to enact curses. Making mages totally distinct while keeping the feel and mystery of awakening was objective #1 and I'm happy to say it was quite successful.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I'm not fond of the Exarchs, and dropping them meant losing the Seers. But I think the Atlantean Orders pick up the slack quite nicely, and it removes any sense that order Mages are somehow fighting the good fight. Though they might not see it that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=838262#post838262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am tempted to write an Art themed after the Supernal Symbol of the Hero, from Heracles to Superman and everything in between. Their Attainments would include the capacity to treat Sleeper witnesses to obvious magic as Sleepwalkers, if the magic is being used in accordance to a heroic persona. I got that idea from the section in the Mage Chronicler's Guide about making Superhero Mages. Their Yantras would include their hero costumes (which might be normal clothes if they want), certain rules of conduct (which can be anti-heroic) and so on. I just don't know if I should go for semi-serious or full Comic Book Silver Age shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do it. As with TKR I will tweak it an add it with attribution. As for semi-serious or full comic book, why choose? Any Mage pursuing the art will be doing so with the conscious knowledge that they are exploring the symbols of heroism, so it should be up to them if they want to go gold, silver, or all pointy with Liefeld pockets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=838262#post838262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, I caught an error: you said Arts replaced Legacies, but you still mentioned the latter in the fifth dot of the Masque Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch, a holdover from a much older draft. Removed that part.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Missed your edit, in my opinion The Doctor would probably have focused around some sort of gung-ho, gentleman explorer, educator adventurer archetype. A lot of focus on The Fool and The Mage as symbols. Yantra being wild gambles, guesses and a general happy-go-lucky dive right in and find out attitude. I could see a Knowing Rote that reveals to him the context of a situation, but only once he's committed to plunging headlong in. All the techno stuff is probably a secondary Art, or some Expanded Style Yantra. He's much more the adventurer than he is a scientist.<br /> <br /> Also I think he's probably Moros. What with his objectivist view and sense of wonder at how humans, nothing more than fleshy plips in the cosmos, can be simultaneously capable of so much and so little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 02-28-2016, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T13:15:33-08:00","id":838773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=838262#post838262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">II am tempted to write an Art themed after the Supernal Symbol of the Hero, from Heracles to Superman and everything in between. Their Attainments would include the capacity to treat Sleeper witnesses to obvious magic as Sleepwalkers, if the magic is being used in accordance to a heroic persona. I got that idea from the section in the Mage Chronicler's Guide about making Superhero Mages. Their Yantras would include their hero costumes (which might be normal clothes if they want), certain rules of conduct (which can be anti-heroic) and so on. I just don't know if I should go for semi-serious or full Comic Book Silver Age shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feast, I'm sorry, I got impatient and had a windfall. Sorry... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On the plus side, here's an <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#heading=h.nu07hv65kt3i\" target=\"_blank\">art</a>. I'd love to hear your thoughts on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T13:48:31-08:00","id":838784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=838773#post838773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feast, I'm sorry, I got impatient and had a windfall. Sorry... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On the plus side, here's an <a href=\"http://&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#heading=h.nu07hv65kt3i&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">art</a>. I'd love to hear your thoughts on it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hey, no worries. Also, thanks for replying to my questions about Mage!Doctor. He's got a lot of different versions and spin-offs, so his Path can be whatever you want with the right phrasing.<br /> <br /> As for the Gold And Silver Caul? The name alone is kickass, and the fact the Diamond sees it as Left-Handed is very in-character. I thought about allowing Hero Mages to borrow the Masque Merit, but you beat me to it. One important thing that's missing is an Attainment for Heroic Items, from Heracle's spoils of battles with monsters to Spider-Man's web-shooters. The other Attainment already turn Sleepers into Sleepwalkers, so maybe this would offer an additional free Reach for spells contained in an Imbued Item or Artifact?<br /> <br /> I thought about adding an Attainment for dealing with Arch-Enemies, but my hunch is to handle that with just narration, so there won't be mechanics forcing it to go this or that way.<br /> <br /> Splendid work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-28-2016, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T16:18:49-08:00","id":838847,"title":"","content":"Another observation about the Gold And Silver Caul. At first, I didn't get why Mastigos was the Resonant Path. To me, it would be Obrimos, because ideal heroes like Superman and Captain America fight for a cause they sincerely believe in, come Hell or high water. But then I remembered that most superheroes have a tragic event in their past that spurs them onward. Those who Awaken to the Watchtower of the Iron Gauntlet have to come to terms with a crucial flaw, no matter how much it hurts, hence the the term Scourging. Some heroes do exactly that, but others wear the trappings and use the powers of a Mastigos without embracing the renewal in agony. Batman is a divisive case. You can say he's a real Mastigos because he rejects a safe and ostentatious life in the ivory tower in order to protect the innocent. Or you can say he's a Banisher who cannot accept a misfortune that wasn't his fault. I'd go as far as to say that he would only become a Mastigos if he stopped fighting crime as Batman.<br /> <br /> I might be running my mouth off into superficiality town, but I thought it was worth mentioning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T20:12:04-08:00","id":838936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=838784#post838784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hey, no worries. Also, thanks for replying to my questions about Mage!Doctor. He's got a lot of different versions and spin-offs, so his Path can be whatever you want with the right phrasing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, each regeneration being a slightly different person basically means he's run the gambit of the Paths. Honestly, including old Who I can't think of a Path he hasn't been.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=838784#post838784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Gold And Silver Caul? The name alone is kickass, and the fact the Diamond sees it as Left-Handed is very in-character. I thought about allowing Hero Mages to borrow the Masque Merit, but you beat me to it. One important thing that's missing is an Attainment for Heroic Items, from Heracle's spoils of battles with monsters to Spider-Man's web-shooters. The other Attainment already turn Sleepers into Sleepwalkers, so maybe this would offer an additional free Reach for spells contained in an Imbued Item or Artifact?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had intended for the Special Technique Attainment to be capable of replicating 'heroic tools' as well. Like claiming the head of a lion and using it as a justification for your heightened strength and tying it to Life 3's Honing the Form. Web launchers would work the same way, perhaps with a Matter/Life spell for creating wires and swinging along them. The examples in the doc clearly don't convey this, I'll modify it for clarity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=838784#post838784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another observation about the Gold And Silver Caul. At first, I didn't get why Mastigos was the Resonant Path. To me, it would be Obrimos, because ideal heroes like Superman and Captain America fight for a cause they sincerely believe in, come Hell or high water. But then I remembered that most superheroes have a tragic event in their past that spurs them onward. Those who Awaken to the Watchtower of the Iron Gauntlet have to come to terms with a crucial flaw, no matter how much it hurts, hence the the term Scourging. Some heroes do exactly that, but others wear the trappings and use the powers of a Mastigos without embracing the renewal in agony. Batman is a divisive case. You can say he's a real Mastigos because he rejects a safe and ostentatious life in the ivory tower in order to protect the innocent. Or you can say he's a Banisher who cannot accept a misfortune that wasn't his fault. I'd go as far as to say that he would only become a Mastigos if he stopped fighting crime as Batman.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sheer range of heroic individuals made Path a hard call, but I figured that what defines heroes universally in fiction isn't necessarily strength or wits, but challenges they face. That said, it's a hard call between Obrimos and Mastigos. The former's themes are Power and Command, while the latter is Transgression and Confrontation. I figured that between the two heroes are defined by the choices they make, not the power with which they archive them. Also, I figured the human angle of heroes, aligned slightly better with the imagery of Mastigos than Obrimos. Really though, the only difference mechanically is that Obrimos pays two extra experiences to join the Art, and they won't even pay that if it's the first Art they learn (their starting Art). I suspect the Art sees most of it's membership from both paths.<br /> <br /> Path matters very little to the character sheet portion of this hack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=838784#post838784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Splendid work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Many thanks.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Any other concepts you'd like to submit? I work best with a touch of inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 02-29-2016, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T03:21:40-08:00","id":841802,"title":"","content":"I had another thought about the Gold And Silver Caul. Silver is a good electric conductor, which can symbolize Forces. Gold never tarnishes, which can symbolize Prime. Those are the Ruling Arcana of the Obrimos. Was that intentional?<br /> <br /> I had another idea for an Art, but it's vague. I thought it was kinda restrictive to only allow martial spellcasting for Arrow members, so the Art focuses on the use of one's own body as a conduit for magic. In addition to martial arts in the style of Iron Fist, the Art would incorporate athleticism in general. Do you wanna be like a Street Fighter character, or use bullet-time parkour like in Mirror's Edge? You can. The Resonant Path would probably be Thyrsus, with a philosophy like that of the Ferrum Refinement. The main Arcana would be Life and Forces, for physical augmentation and chi attacks. Mind and Fate would also be used to improve tactical awareness. Poses and signature moves would be Yantras all over the place. Attainments should help with Paradox mitigation.<br /> <br /> The problem with allowing this Art is that it could make the Arrow look kinda redundant. Joining that Order could give more control over your magic instead, especially if used in a martial or law-enforcing capacity. Another issue is the whole Quiescence/Dissonance thing, which can make this kind of spellcasting a huge risk.<br /> <br /> What do you think, Pendragon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-04-2016, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T10:58:00-08:00","id":841998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=841802#post841802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had another thought about the Gold And Silver Caul. Silver is a good electric conductor, which can symbolize Forces. Gold never tarnishes, which can symbolize Prime. Those are the Ruling Arcana of the Obrimos. Was that intentional?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gold and Silver thing was a reference to comics mostly, though it's spendidly mage-like of you to find other valuable symbolism in the words <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=841802#post841802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had another idea for an Art, but it's vague. I thought it was kinda restrictive to only allow martial spellcasting for Arrow members, so the Art focuses on the use of one's own body as a conduit for magic. In addition to martial arts in the style of Iron Fist, the Art would incorporate athleticism in general. Do you wanna be like a Street Fighter character, or use bullet-time parkour like in Mirror's Edge? You can. The Resonant Path would probably be Thyrsus, with a philosophy like that of the Ferrum Refinement. The main Arcana would be Life and Forces, for physical augmentation and chi attacks. Mind and Fate would also be used to improve tactical awareness. Poses and signature moves would be Yantras all over the place. Attainments should help with Paradox mitigation.<br /> <br /> The problem with allowing this Art is that it could make the Arrow look kinda redundant. Joining that Order could give more control over your magic instead, especially if used in a martial or law-enforcing capacity. Another issue is the whole Quiescence/Dissonance thing, which can make this kind of spellcasting a huge risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries about making the Arrow &quot;redundant&quot;. The Adamant Arrow is a social distinction, not a magical one. Indeed, and perhaps I should make this more clear in the doc &quot;Guardian of the Veil&quot; or &quot;Adamant Arrow&quot; are not viable Art choices. Under this hack Orders don't provide Rotes or Yantra just for being part of them, they provide access to Arts unique to the order (which in turn give Rotes and Yantra), Metamagical merits like Masques, Egregore and Adamant Hand, and social advantages like Status, Contacts and Allies. Indeed, in older drafts I had an order affiliation section for each Art, but dropped it for the sake of flexibility (e.g. storytellers get to decide which arts cleave to which orders, and which cross boundaries or stand alone). That all said, certain arts clearly nod towards certain Orders. Shepherds of the Flock, your friendly neighborhood thought police, definitely fall under Guardians or the Silver Ladder, and a martial art Art (heh) like the one you've proposed would likely favor either Arrows or Traditionalists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=841802#post841802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think, Pendragon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, as for the art itself, martial arts is definitely a fit and one I've been meaning to get on the list. The only real stopping point is how broad the concept is. Martial Arts take different forms in difference cultures and Arts are supposed to have at least a slight cultural connection (because as much as the Diamond wants to be culture agnostic, it's very hard to remove culture from people). I'm thinking though a Wuxia Art, possibly with some heavy Neidan (internal alchemy) leanings should find its way on the list.<br /> <br /> Basically, I think it's a good idea.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#heading=h.lq81lff73lt5\" target=\"_blank\">First stab at the concept</a>. I went for a very standard, Akashic Brotherhood style Art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 03-04-2016, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T19:48:21-08:00","id":842835,"title":"","content":"I really like the Taiji Neidan! You're very good at this. Tying their Paradox mitigation Attainment to codes of honor helps to enhance the monk feel. Martial Synergy is elegantly broad, but it works especially well with Armed Defense, Unarmed Defense and Light Weapons. The weapon would probably be a wooden staff. I am also fond of a greaves + gauntlets combo made of stone that the Mage can wield easily because of Life Perfecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T18:55:41-07:00","id":865262,"title":"","content":"I read your Mage house rules again. While I do support the elimination of Ruling and Inferior Arcana, I am fond of the idea that you must seek out teachers of a specific Path to become a Master yourself. However, if I limit the dots you can have in this or that Arcana, I'd be bringing back the Ruling and Inferior division. On the other hand, an Arcane Experience discount seems underwhelming. What else do you think could encourage them to do that?<br /> <br /> Also, once again on the topic of the Gold And Silver Caul...is just me, or would <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-the-nwod?p=852643#post852643\">Saitama</a> </b>count as an &quot;Arch-Cheater&quot; attuned to the Realm Of Keter and a practitioner of the aforementioned Mystic Art? The three years of training he did after saving a boy from a crab monster <a href=\"http://wheresmysammich.com/images/77563.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><b>couldn't possibly have given him godlike power</b></a>, which is pointed out in the show. Unless that training, loss of hair, apparent immunity to fame and learning the true meaning of heroism somehow count as his &quot;Second Awakening&quot; + Quintessence. You can watch <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qHOfZF7YExk\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this video</b></a> for a longer analysis.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Could you please update my username in the parts of your Mystic Arts and Demon House Rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-13-2016, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T19:06:29-07:00","id":865265,"title":"","content":"I've only skimmed through your Mage 2E stuff, so far. But I'm liking a lot of the stuff that I'm seeing there. Expect some of the stuff you got to be used by me when I get to doing my own set of House Rules for the Awakened.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As always, great work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T22:04:56-07:00","id":865326,"title":"","content":"Power and Command are the themes of the Obrimos in 2ED, right? With great power, comes great responsibility. This makes me think that if Spider-Man is not an Acanthus, he is an Obrimos.<br /> <br /> All in all, Mastigos and Obrimos are two sides of the same coin when it comes to heroism, as Pendragon pointed out. I think of these different symbols and ideals as complementary in a special way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T12:15:35-07:00","id":865645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=865262#post865262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read your Mage house rules again. While I do support the elimination of Ruling and Inferior Arcana, I am fond of the idea that you must seek out teachers of a specific Path to become a Master yourself. However, if I limit the dots you can have in this or that Arcana, I'd be bringing back the Ruling and Inferior division. On the other hand, an Arcane Experience discount seems underwhelming. What else do you think could encourage them to do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Experience is something I've been toying around with recently, and not just for Mage. Like you I don't want to lose that Master-Student relationship Mage provides, but I also don't want to 'favor' certain Arcana or utterly hamstring independent Mages (cutting them off from Arts and Rotes is a pretty heavy hit already). What I'm thinking I'll do, going forward is break experience down by Mundane and Arcane. Mundane can be spent on Attributes, Skills, and Merits, stuff everyone can buy. Arcane Experience is spent on Arcana, Rotes &amp; Attainments, things only Mages get. Then, taking a note from Exalted, Gnosis isn't bought, but rises naturally by 1 for every 5 or10 (I'm undecided on the amount) Arcane Experiences you accrue.<br /> <br /> As for what a Mentor can provide: Rotes and Attainments, which are both huge. The hacks make Rotes stupendously powerful, and Attainments should be highly enticing to anyone who wants to spice up their magic. Mentors also provide guidance and direction, which will rapidly translate into Experiences Mundane and Arcane. But as for Arcana, just as you cannot forcibly Awaken a Sleeper, you cannot beat enlightenment into a Mage. That's between him and the Supernal.<br /> <br /> (Note: I'm planning to do this for other splats as well. Vampires get Kindred Experience, Werewolves get Spirit Experiences, etc. Which nicely solves the somewhat common issue of players dumping all their Experiences into splat traits, or feeling disappointed that they have to 'waste' exp on things like skills).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=865262#post865262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, once again on the topic of the Gold And Silver Caul...is just me, or would <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-the-nwod?p=852643#post852643\">Saitama</a> </b>count as an &quot;Arch-Cheater&quot; attuned to the Realm Of Keter and a practitioner of the aforementioned Mystic Art? The three years of training he did after saving a boy from a crab monster <a href=\"http://wheresmysammich.com/images/77563.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><b>couldn't possibly have given him godlike power</b></a>, which is pointed out in the show. Unless that training, loss of hair, apparent immunity to fame and learning the true meaning of heroism somehow count as his &quot;Second Awakening&quot; + Quintessence. You can watch <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qHOfZF7YExk\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this video</b></a> for a longer analysis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I love me some OP Man, and you could most certainly spin up a Saitama like character. But honestly that's not really the sort of heroic vibe I had in mind when writing that Art. I was more in the American comic mindset, notably Morrison or Moore. I ended up settling on Mastigos not because heroes are inherently Mastigosian, but because Mastigos seemed the most likely Path to favor inventing elaborate second identities and living outside the law.<br /> <br /> Really though the only difference between and Obrimos taking the Art and a Mastigos is the Mastigos gets it for 2xp less, and that's only if it isn't the character's first art, in which case it's free.<br /> <br /> On the topic of Anime, I draw <b>a lot </b>of Mage inspiration from Kara no Kyoukai, which is probably the most CofD anime ever produced. The Ufotable adaptations of the Fate/ franchise also hit the nail on the head. Beyond those there is also Shin Sekai Yori (a horror anime) and, though not strictly about sorcery, Ghost in the Shell. And, as ashamed as I am to say it, the Monogatari Series (Bakemonogatari, Nisemonogatari, etc.) also tend to color my take on Awakening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=865262#post865262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Could you please update my username in the parts of your Mystic Arts and Demon House Rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 04-14-2016, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T15:45:21-07:00","id":869718,"title":"","content":"I like that idea from Exalted of raising the Powerstat for every 5 or 10 Supernatural Experiences. However, I've been wondering how each splat would acquire those. I noted what seem to be the official guidelines, plus my ideas. Are they similar to yours?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Vampire:</b> Struggles and triumphs in the Danse Macabre, learning the lore of your Covenant, encountering different types of vampires, controlling the Beast with great effort or letting it guide you for now.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf:</b> There's already quite a lot of guidance in the Renown system, but perhaps you could also advance by deliberately going to the extremes of Harmony and staying there for a good while.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage:</b> Mysteries, Obsessions, learning from your mentor, teaching a student and establishing yourself within an Order. I'd like to see a special type of Aspiration similar to Obsessions, but meant for increasing Wisdom.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean:</b> Milestones, Athanors and Vitriol Experiences are looking good, from the few teasers we had thus far.<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling:</b> Facing difficulties while upholding Pledges or due to breaking them, using your Approaches to evade capture, exploring the Hedge and the Skein, acquiring titles in your Court, helping newly escaped changelings, discovering Loyalists and confronting them, cause problems for your Fetch or learn from them<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter:</b> Tactics and Practical Experiences work nicely with the fluff. I'm interested in how 2ED will handle Tells and Integrity.<br /> <br /> <b>Geist:</b> Pursuing your Archetypes, joining Krewes and creating your own, investigate the past of your Geist and other Sin-Eaters, explore the Underworld and its secrets<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy: </b>I don't know much about it, but your ideas for Memory and Monuments are great. Do any of the supplements have some minimal crunchy guidance for Apotheosis?<br /> <br /> <b>Demon:</b> Cover Experiences and the Pact system work together nicely. I'd like something that complements the Experiences you get while fulfilling your Agendas and can be spent on Primum, Embeds, Exploits and Demonic Merits.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> The inherent advantages built for cross-over are a good start, as are the Beats given by the Satiety Conditions. More guidelines for spreading your Legend and becoming the Apex would be useful. More info on how Beasts traverse the Primordial Dream, the rest of the Astral and other Invisible Realms is something many people want, it seems.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-20-2016, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T08:48:09-07:00","id":875686,"title":"","content":"Did you remove that part that part that gave you bonuses and penalties based on how you became a Mage? I could have sworn it used to be there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:02:03-07:00","id":878370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=875686#post875686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you remove that part that part that gave you bonuses and penalties based on how you became a Mage? I could have sworn it used to be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did. The whole Tarot Suit awakening approach didn't really fit with Awakening (I ported it to Ascension instead). I have, however, been revisiting the concept of Enlightenment Conditions, mental quirks Mages take upon awakening that generate beats and encourage the players to play up the whole lucid madness aspect of Mages. Conditions like:<br /> <br /> <b>Storied</b><br /> You\u2019ve traversed the paths of the Lunargent Thorn, and learned The Truth. The world is not more than an elaborate fiction and you are but a character within this text. You understand that the world abides literary rules: acts, arcs and conflicts, and that people, knowingly or not, play out little roles.<br /> <b>Possible Sources</b>: Acanthus Awakening<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: None<br /> <b>Beat</b>: Whenever you knowingly take detrimental action 'in character' for the sake of 'the story', or make seemingly irrational assumptions about people or the world based on literary rules.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Actually, I could use some ideas for Conditions. I've got about eight right now, which simply isn't enough. So if anyone wants to pitch a few I'm all ears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 04-29-2016, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:45:45-07:00","id":878406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=878392#post878392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure thing. I might make a few changes, Valeren doesn't really read like a 2e Discipline, but I will definitely add a prominent link to your original version.<br /> <br /> If there's anything else you want to pitch or discuss feel free, though you should probably do it my homebrew thread (it'd be sorta threadcapping here)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bI initially had Valeren as a Bloodline gift, however, the Gui Ren, non-Kindred vampires, have access to the Discipline, and I felt like 'giving the Beast sight' was tangentially thematic enough, if exotic. But, I understand, the hesitancy of adding new Disciplines. I originally had them as their own Requiem clan (and every clan has a proprietary Discipline.) However, Dominate works with the very mental focus they have, and was my initialy Disciplien slot before I decided to keep Valeren as a Discipline.<br /> <br /> I would add;<br /> <br /> SENSE VITALITY<br /> When using <i>Uncanny Perception</i>, a Salubri adds the following questions to the list that can be asked;<ul><li>How many health levels of damage the subject has suffered;</li> <li>How full the subject's Vitae pool is (if a vampire) or how many blood points she has left in her system (if a mortal or other blood-bearing form of life);</li> <li>Any diseases in the subject's bloodstream, such as haemophilia or HIV.</li> <li>Any Conditions related to infirmity of the body or spiritual malaise, such as soullessness or possession by an ephemeral entity</li> </ul>And include 'Anesthetic Touch' as a Dominate 2, Auspex 1 Devotion, and Ending the Watch as a Dominate 5, Auspex 4. Shepherd's Watch becomes Majesty 3, Resilience 2, and Unburdening the Soul becomes Auspex 5, Dominate 4. That was the original anyways. Burning Touch was not retained as a Devotion, but everything else made it was Devotions, or Bloodline gifts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:51:41-07:00","id":878411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=878406#post878406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI initially had Valeren as a Bloodline gift, however, the Gui Ren, non-Kindred vampires, have access to the Discipline, and I felt like 'giving the Beast sight' was tangentially thematic enough, if exotic. But, I understand, the hesitancy of adding new Disciplines. I originally had them as their own Requiem clan (and every clan has a proprietary Discipline.) However, Dominate works with the very mental focus they have, and was my initialy Disciplien slot before I decided to keep Valeren as a Discipline.<br /> <br /> I would add;<br /> <br /> SENSE VITALITY<br /> When using <i>Uncanny Perception</i>, a Salubri adds the following questions to the list that can be asked;<ul><li>How many health levels of damage the subject has suffered;</li> <li>How full the subject's Vitae pool is (if a vampire) or how many blood points she has left in her system (if a mortal or other blood-bearing form of life);</li> <li>Any diseases in the subject's bloodstream, such as haemophilia or HIV.</li> <li>Any Conditions related to infirmity of the body or spiritual malaise, such as soullessness or possession by an ephemeral entity</li> </ul>And include 'Anesthetic Touch' as a Dominate 2, Auspex 1 Devotion, and Ending the Watch as a Dominate 5, Auspex 4. Shepherd's Watch becomes Majesty 3, Resilience 2, and Unburdening the Soul becomes Auspex 5, Dominate 4. That was the original anyways. Burning Touch was not retained as a Devotion, but everything else made it was Devotions, or Bloodline gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely going to go through and get more of that writeup in there as Bloodline Devotions. As for the Discipline, its a fine adaptation, I've just got really strict personal standards on what a Discipline should look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T21:00:33-07:00","id":878418,"title":"","content":"Indeed, it's a fine... hack of a hack of a hack? Heh. It keeps the same flavor. It's good","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T14:51:32-07:00","id":880496,"title":"","content":"With the release of Mage 2e to Beast Backers I'm finally able to dump a finalized (well, 1.0) version of my 2e Hacks. Though honestly the release of the book didn't change much, DaveB's spoilers were so complete that I was able to make an extremely accurate assessment of the final version. Or at least accurate enough for my liking. However, the document remains quite long (in no small part due to the pages and pages of Arts), so I will summarize the biggest changes here:<ul><li>No more Ruling or Inferior Arcana. All Spells, even Rotes (though not Praxis), cost a point of Mana to cast.</li> <li>Rotes can be purchased for spells even if you don't meet the Arcana prerequisites, and give you Free Reach equal to your dots in the spell's primary Arcana.</li> <li>All non-Praxis spells require at least one Yantra during casting or they suffer Paradox.</li> <li>Legacies and Arcana based attainments are out, replaced with Mystic Arts. Arts similar to Legacies in many ways, they grant Yantra, Oblations and Attainments, but don't have Gnosis limitations. Arts are where you can gain Sympathetic Magic, Mage Armor and other Arcana based powers.</li> <li>The Seers are out, the Diamond and the Free Assemblies don't get along well, and Nameless Orders hold considerably more sway. This is most setting stuff, little in the way of rules here.</li> <li>There are also a number of modified merits, Obligations as an alternative for those who don't want obsessions, and a little hack for playing Mages who awaken by birth (retooled Proximi).</li> </ul>As always, this is a personal doc shared here for those who are interested, or simply want to pick through for inspiration. Constructive comments are welcome, as are requests. If you simply don't like the hack that's fine, but please don't shit post, just ignore it and enjoy Mage 2e when it releases to the general public on Wednesday. It is a splendid work.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Oh, right, link: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...LWs9Z-SI/edit#</a><br /> <br /> <b>Edit x2: </b>Also added Enlightenment Conditions, which encourage Mages to act...a little crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-02-2016, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T17:16:37-07:00","id":881369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=880496#post880496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the release of Mage 2e to Beast Backers I'm finally able to dump a finalized (well, 1.0) version of my 2e Hacks. Though honestly the release of the book didn't change much, DaveB's spoilers were so complete that I was able to make an extremely accurate assessment of the final version. Or at least accurate enough for my liking. However, the document remains quite long (in no small part due to the pages and pages of Arts), so I will summarize the biggest changes here:<ul><li>No more Ruling or Inferior Arcana. All Spells, even Rotes (though not Praxis), cost a point of Mana to cast.</li> <li>Rotes can be purchased for spells even if you don't meet the Arcana prerequisites, and give you Free Reach equal to your dots in the spell's primary Arcana.</li> <li>All non-Praxis spells require at least one Yantra during casting or they suffer Paradox.</li> <li>Legacies and Arcana based attainments are out, replaced with Mystic Arts. Arts similar to Legacies in many ways, they grant Yantra, Oblations and Attainments, but don't have Gnosis limitations. Arts are where you can gain Sympathetic Magic, Mage Armor and other Arcana based powers.</li> <li>The Seers are out, the Diamond and the Free Assemblies don't get along well, and Nameless Orders hold considerably more sway. This is most setting stuff, little in the way of rules here.</li> <li>There are also a number of modified merits, Obligations as an alternative for those who don't want obsessions, and a little hack for playing Mages who awaken by birth (retooled Proximi).</li> </ul>As always, this is a personal doc shared here for those who are interested, or simply want to pick through for inspiration. Constructive comments are welcome, as are requests. If you simply don't like the hack that's fine, but please don't shit post, just ignore it and enjoy Mage 2e when it releases to the general public on Wednesday. It is a splendid work.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Oh, right, link: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...LWs9Z-SI/edit#</a><br /> <br /> <b>Edit x2: </b>Also added Enlightenment Conditions, which encourage Mages to act...a little crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely seeing some of these hacks being ported over to my own once I get started on them. Specifically the Enlightenment Conditions, Obligations, (most of) the hacks for Proximi, and some of the modified Merits. The Mystic Art, Expanded Style, and Unified Arts Merits, though, might be something I'd retool for my own interpretation of Thaumaturges (and perhaps Proximi) once I've worked out some issues on my mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T17:38:28-07:00","id":881381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=878418#post878418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, it's a fine... hack of a hack of a hack? Heh. It keeps the same flavor. It's good</div> </div> </div> </div>Updated the entry a bit, and took my own stab at Unburden the Soul. Let me know what you think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T23:44:42-07:00","id":882618,"title":"","content":"Got a copy of Mage 2E here, and I went straight to the section on Obsessions. Are we going to be expecting some additions to your Mage 2E House Rules, now that we have an idea on how they're handled?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T01:04:13-07:00","id":882655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=882618#post882618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got a copy of Mage 2E here, and I went straight to the section on Obsessions. Are we going to be expecting some additions to your Mage 2E House Rules, now that we have an idea on how they're handled?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't have any plans for Obsessions, I think the text handles them well enough. I did add Obligations as an alternative option, which function in essentially the same way as Obsessions, but are focused more on magical debts and duties, for Mages who have taken a more 'magic as a responsibility' approach to the game.<br /> <br /> Did you have something in mind?<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: I'll also use this post to note a couple other changes:<ul><li>Added modified Withstand rules (courtesy of Falco1029)</li> <li>Added several Sleeper merits, including a sleeper sub-template called Imbued, mortals who have been magically modified to serve as Imbued Objects, and bear the weight of duty or madness (or both) in exchange for power.</li> <li>Renamed Enlightenment Conditions to Paradigm (cribbing Ascension in name only), and an Appendix of Proximi Curses, most of which are from actual play.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T02:08:30-07:00","id":882688,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I vastly prefer your version of Proximis (and Thaumaturges) to the one in Second Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T02:30:53-07:00","id":882699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=882688#post882688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I vastly prefer your version of Proximis (and Thaumaturges) to the one in Second Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that's why I put out the docs.<br /> <br /> Though between 1e and 2e I made the call up upgrade Proximi to full Mages, rather than attempt to differentiate between the two increasingly similar splats. Indeed a number of my Mage changes came from this, namely the Rote change (e.g. Rotes can be learned without meeting their prerequisite Arcana) which came mostly from my desire to preserve the 141 Proximi spells I wrote.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>As for Thaumaturges, not sure if I'll revive the idea of Colleges and spheres, at least not in the way I'd written them for 1e. But the effect can be amalgamated by choosing the right Art (a number of which were takes on the Colleges I wrote).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-05-2016, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T03:04:14-07:00","id":882714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=882699#post882699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed a number of my Mage changes came from this, namely the Rote change (e.g. Rotes can be learned without meeting their prerequisite Arcana) which came mostly from my desire to preserve the 141 Proximi spells I wrote.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might need to take a moment comparing that hack with what's been written for Rotes in Mage 2E. But I do admit that I'm in favor of this, as well as a hack that allows for Mages to <i>create</i> Rotes if they possess the prerequisite Arcana dots. That way, Master Mages can have a more potent benefit at five dots in an Arcanum, like perhaps the rote quality to all Rote spells stemming from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T11:51:55-07:00","id":883071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=882714#post882714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might need to take a moment comparing that hack with what's been written for Rotes in Mage 2E. But I do admit that I'm in favor of this, as well as a hack that allows for Mages to <i>create</i> Rotes if they possess the prerequisite Arcana dots. That way, Master Mages can have a more potent benefit at five dots in an Arcanum, like perhaps the rote quality to all Rote spells stemming from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would a comparison breakdown help?<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <u>Core Rotes</u><br /> <b>Cost: </b>-1 Mana (minimum 0)<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Gnosis + Arcana + Skill<br /> <b>Reach: </b>6 - Highest Arcana in the Spell<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Caster must have all the Arcana involved in the spell at the levels of the spell.<br /> <b>Experiences: </b>1<br /> - Can only be made by Masters<br /> - The Master who made the Rote gains the Rote Quality on the roll.<br /> <br /> <u>Hack Rotes</u><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Mana<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Gnosis + Arcana + Skill<br /> <b>Reach: </b>One Per Dot you Possess in the Spell's Primary Arcana<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> <b>Experiences: </b>1<br /> - Can only be made by Masters</div>I toyed around with letting non-Masters create Rotes, but in the end I decided against it. I feared it would undermine the importance of true masters in the Awakened world and lead Rotes to feeling slightly less special. Beyond that, the above hack has worked out well in actual play. My players have universally enjoyed the access to 'high tier' tricks and like that they don't need to invest ten plus experiences into an Arcana just to get the single effect they area after. The hack has also lead to some pretty great scenes, like a relatively novice character birthing a god-damned sun to defeat what was otherwise and unstoppable foe.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the universal access to Rotes makes being a Rote thief, who collects Rotes, far more viable. And justifies why Orders are so protective of their most powerful Rotes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T12:22:50-07:00","id":883101,"title":"","content":"So, do you plan to still keep your old Half-Awake hacks up, or will you delete them now that you've decided on a new direction? <br /> <br /> Also, a thought on an Art idea; considering that she appears to be somewhat active in the world, and there's already Arts for the G-M and the Principle, is it possible there's a Pandemonium-favored Prelacy Art themed around the Dark Mother? Mind seems obvious, maybe also Space?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T12:32:18-07:00","id":883110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=883101#post883101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, do you plan to still keep your old Half-Awake hacks up, or will you delete them now that you've decided on a new direction?</div> </div> </div> </div>But of course. No skin off my back to keep the 1e docs up. And I'll probably retool the Rotes I made for 2e Proximi sometime, release them as a separate doc just composed of cool spells. I'll be damned if 160+ written spells go to waste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=883101#post883101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a thought on an Art idea; considering that she appears to be somewhat active in the world, and there's already Arts for the G-M and the Principle, is it possible there's a Pandemonium-favored Prelacy Art themed around the Dark Mother? Mind seems obvious, maybe also Space?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps an Art of Primordial Sages, who delve the depths of the human mind and seek to learn the nature of the Primordial Dream. At their best they are wardens who help reign in the Nightmare, but all too many fall prey to their own Obsessions and seek the Dark Mother to vindicate their own vices...yes I think I can work with that.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>This actually bears a lot of similarity to the Maleficia Art I wrote, which itself was based on the Baali Proximi I'd written prior. But this is a more interesting direction, I might go revise that Art into this one.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit #2: </b>Yes, that's a much better take on the Art. Thank you ZC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-05-2016, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T17:15:56-07:00","id":883324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=883071#post883071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a comparison breakdown help?<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <u>Core Rotes</u><br /> <b>Cost: </b>-1 Mana (minimum 0)<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Gnosis + Arcana + Skill<br /> <b>Reach: </b>6 - Highest Arcana in the Spell<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Caster must have all the Arcana involved in the spell at the levels of the spell.<br /> <b>Experiences: </b>1<br /> - Can only be made by Masters<br /> - The Master who made the Rote gains the Rote Quality on the roll.<br /> <br /> <u>Hack Rotes</u><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Mana<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Gnosis + Arcana + Skill<br /> <b>Reach: </b>One Per Dot you Possess in the Spell's Primary Arcana<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> <b>Experiences: </b>1<br /> - Can only be made by Masters</div>I toyed around with letting non-Masters create Rotes, but in the end I decided against it. I feared it would undermine the importance of true masters in the Awakened world and lead Rotes to feeling slightly less special. Beyond that, the above hack has worked out well in actual play. My players have universally enjoyed the access to 'high tier' tricks and like that they don't need to invest ten plus experiences into an Arcana just to get the single effect they area after. The hack has also lead to some pretty great scenes, like a relatively novice character birthing a god-damned sun to defeat what was otherwise and unstoppable foe.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the universal access to Rotes makes being a Rote thief, who collects Rotes, far more viable. And justifies why Orders are so protective of their most powerful Rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that definitely gives me a better idea of how the rule hack works. And the image of a novice Mage being able to conjure a freaking <i>SUN</i> IS awesome, I admit. Also, lovin the fact that having Order-specific Rotes get stolen by an ambitious Mage is a more serious issue with these mechanics.<br /> <br /> I might toy around with it, though, to fit with some of the hacks I'm also thinking up. Which include....<br /> <br /> * Mages <i>can</i> cast spells from Arcana they have no dots in. However, they take a -3 Unskilled penalty to the dice roll. (Adapted from both the To the Limit Rule from Tome of Mysteries, and some of the rules for group spellcasting in Mage 2E)<br /> * Mages who score an Exceptional Success in a spell may add an extra Spell Factor, plus one for every two extra successes. (This can fit well with the advantages of Praxes in the core, which are Exceptional at three successes*<br /> * Mages who cast Praxes treat <i>all</i> Magical Tools as Dedicated. (something I'm bringing back from the Yantra previews, in addition to the aforementioned exceptional threshold benefit).<br /> * Mages can have more than one Dedicated Tool (still thinking whether I should tie it to Gnosis, or make it a Merit that can be rated at one, three, or five dots).<br /> * Praxes are not subject to Paradoxical Casting.<br /> <br /> As the last point shows, I'm also adapting some of the Paradoxical Casting rules from ToM to make Mana costs a soft requirement for spells. Opting not to spend Mana for a spell from a Common/Inferior Arcanum leaves you with a (small number of) Paradox dice that can potentially skew it from the effect you intended. All-Out Magic from Armory Reloaded is also a yes.<br /> <br /> I'm also trying to differentiate Praxes and Rotes further from one another, and perhaps even work out how to use both together. Still not sure whether or not it should be a Rule Hack that allows it, by default. But I can also see a one-dot Merit working. I probably might end up calling it Rote Mastery, and have the Praxis version of the spell, and a single Rote in it as prerequisites.<br /> <br /> For Rotes, though, I'm wondering whether I should go with the 2E core or your rule hack for free Reach. I can probably let the 1 Mana cost be kept for a Mage if he does not yet have high enough dots in the right Arcana, after which he can perform it at no cost. And for Praxes, meanwhile, maybe I could tie their free Reach to their Gnosis dots, or half of it (rounded up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-05-2016, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T01:21:17-07:00","id":883566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=883324#post883324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that definitely gives me a better idea of how the rule hack works. And the image of a novice Mage being able to conjure a freaking <i>SUN</i> IS awesome, I admit. Also, lovin the fact that having Order-specific Rotes get stolen by an ambitious Mage is a more serious issue with these mechanics.<br /> <br /> For Rotes, though, I'm wondering whether I should go with the 2E core or your rule hack for free Reach. I can probably let the 1 Mana cost be kept for a Mage if he does not yet have high enough dots in the right Arcana, after which he can perform it at no cost. And for Praxes, meanwhile, maybe I could tie their free Reach to their Gnosis dots, or half of it (rounded up).</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it would it help if I explained my reasoning for the assorted changes:<ul><li><b>Cost</b>: This one was pure preference. I like my Mages casting, but not all the damn time, and wanted to emphasize the importance of mana and hollows. I deemed that, given the boost in power, Rotes could use to be cut back somewhere, Cost was the obvious choice. As an added benefit, along with the removal of Ruling Arcana, this lets Praxis shine as the only spells Mages can cast freely. My players used their Praxis non-stop, which further focused and differentiated the characters.</li> <li><b>Reach: </b>This change was for two reasons. First and foremost, with everyone having access to Rotes I needed to differentiate between characters who were actually good at the Arcana and those that merely dabbled. Sure Arcana is already in the dice pool, but 1-5 dice seemed too little, especially given that they could be offset with Yantra easily enough. Reach was the other clear option, and from experience the hack does a good job of making it clear who the real masters are. Speaking of masters, point two I wanted there to be some Reach based benefit to learning a Rote as a master. Making it possible for 5 dot spells to be cast safely by making them Rotes fit the bill.</li> <li><b>Prerequisites: </b>You already hit this nail on the head, the removal of prereqs gives the Orders a much clearer reason to covet their Rotes, and lets players (and storytellers) give mages interesting powers without having to give them, say, five dots of Time and everything that comes with it.</li> </ul>I can say, with confidence, that all these changes went over really well. My players were eager to invest in Rotes and prefered casting Rotes over relying on standard Creative Thaumatugy whenever possible. They are just a better value for the mana. The above Sun example also showcased why novices shouldn't be given five dot Rotes, as when the spell was used he had nowhere near enough Reach to hit the scale he was aiming for and ended up nearly killing himself to soak the Paradox.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Hot damn, I forgot to add my Paradox hack to the doc. How the hell did I forget that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-06-2016, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T01:42:16-07:00","id":883576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=883566#post883566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it would it help if I explained my reasoning for the assorted changes:<ul><li><b>Cost</b>: This one was pure preference. I like my Mages casting, but not all the damn time, and wanted to emphasize the importance of mana and hollows. I deemed that, given the boost in power, Rotes could use to be cut back somewhere, Cost was the obvious choice. As an added benefit, along with the removal of Ruling Arcana, this lets Praxis shine as the only spells Mages can cast freely. My players used their Praxis non-stop, which further focused and differentiated the characters.</li> <li><b>Reach: </b>This change was for two reasons. First and foremost, with everyone having access to Rotes I needed to differentiate between characters who were actually good at the Arcana and those that merely dabbled. Sure Arcana is already in the dice pool, but 1-5 dice seemed too little, especially given that they could be offset with Yantra easily enough. Reach was the other clear option, and from experience the hack does a good job of making it clear who the real masters are. Speaking of masters, point two I wanted there to be some Reach based benefit to learning a Rote as a master. Making it possible for 5 dot spells to be cast safely by making them Rotes fit the bill.</li> <li><b>Prerequisites: </b>You already hit this nail on the head, the removal of prereqs gives the Orders a much clearer reason to covet their Rotes, and lets players (and storytellers) give mages interesting powers without having to give them, say, five dots of Time and everything that comes with it.</li> </ul>I can say, with confidence, that all these changes went over really well. My players were eager to invest in Rotes and prefered casting Rotes over relying on standard Creative Thaumatugy whenever possible. They are just a better value for the mana. The above Sun example also showcased why novices shouldn't be given five dot Rotes, as when the spell was used he had nowhere near enough Reach to hit the scale he was aiming for and ended up nearly killing himself to soak the Paradox.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Hot damn, I forgot to add my Paradox hack to the doc. How the hell did I forget that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that definitely gives me a better idea on how to handle my hacks.<br /> <br /> I might let Rotes cost 1 Mana, at minimum, and apply the reduction once a Mage meets the prerequisite Arcana. I might go a different direction, though, with differentiating Praxes. Especially since I'm very receptive to the idea of a very skilled Mage being able to synergize a spell he knows, by heart, with the benefits afforded by a Rote's encoded workings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T01:44:15-07:00","id":883580,"title":"","content":"PenDragon, I just saw the completed Salubri, and I am impressed. That is an extremely faithful rendition. I'm happy about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T01:50:50-07:00","id":883585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=883576#post883576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that definitely gives me a better idea on how to handle my hacks.<br /> <br /> I might let Rotes cost 1 Mana, at minimum, and apply the reduction once a Mage meets the prerequisite Arcana. I might go a different direction, though, with differentiating Praxes. Especially since I'm very receptive to the idea of a very skilled Mage being able to synergize a spell he knows, by heart, with the benefits afforded by a Rote's encoded workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you aren't interested in making casting more costly then I'd suggest going with the standard &quot;Rotes cost one less Mana&quot;, unless, as you've already proposed, the caster doesn't meet the prereqs. In which case the price would be a good way to set apart those who understand the theory and those who are just going through the motions.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if you don't do the cost change, Praxis would need a different direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T01:57:11-07:00","id":883591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=883580#post883580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PenDragon, I just saw the completed Salubri, and I am impressed. That is an extremely faithful rendition. I'm happy about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's genuinely relieving to hear, I was worried that the changes would be insulting. I tried to keep the original flavor and function as much as possible, while taking up slightly less space (I'm not constrained by word count like standard books, but I've got to give myself some limits).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T02:08:24-07:00","id":883600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=883585#post883585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, if you don't do the cost change, Praxis would need a different direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Well, I have tentative notes put together. Allow me to post them here for easier comparison....<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Praxes:</b><br /> * Consider all magical tools as Dedicated (actual Dedicated Tools double their benefits).<br /> * Cost one less Mana to cast, unless the Mage does not meet the prerequisite Arcana.<br /> * Do not suffer from Paradoxical Casting.<br /> * Any extra Reach in excess of the Mage's Wisdom does not add +1 to Paradox rolls.<br /> * Score an Exceptional Success at three successes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rotes:</b><br /> * Add dots in an associated Skill as a Yantra to the dice pool.<br /> * Cost one less Mana to cast, unless the Mage does not meet the prerequisite Arcana.<br /> * If a Rote's Skill is a specialty of the Mage's Order, add bonus dice equal to half the Mage's dots in Order Status (rounded up).<br /> * Reduces Paradox dice by half the Rote's associated Skill dots (rounded up).<br /> * The Signature Nimbus of the caster is indistinct, hiding the caster\u2019s identity unless another Mage fully Scrutinizes the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:12:30-07:00","id":883963,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this is the right place to post this, but I made a Mystical Art for PenDragon's Mage 2e thing and I would like to know what you guys think of it.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tlXQAaya_YU4PDBI7YBKEMmPQUmyM61Uz1JPtozJImg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tlXQAaya_YU4PDBI7YBKEMmPQUmyM61Uz1JPtozJImg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tlXQAaya_YU4PDBI7YBKEMmPQUmyM61Uz1JPtozJImg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tlXQAaya_YU4PDBI7YBKEMmPQUmyM61Uz1JPtozJImg/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:24:38-07:00","id":883976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=883963#post883963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this is the right place to post this, but I made a Mystical Art for PenDragon's Mage 2e thing and I would like to know what you guys think of it.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tlXQAaya_YU4PDBI7YBKEMmPQUmyM61Uz1JPtozJImg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I bleeding love it. Any objections if I tweak it ever so slightly and drop it in my doc? With proper attribution of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-06-2016, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:26:21-07:00","id":883980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=883976#post883976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bleeding love it. Any objects if I tweak it ever so slightly and drop it in my doc? With proper attribution of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please go right ahead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T19:44:11-07:00","id":884270,"title":"","content":"Little Mage hack update:<br /> <br /> After some consideration on the words of DaveB regarding the Withstood mechanic I've opted to drop my Withstand hacks (which allowed characters to use Supernal advantage) in place of a universal Clash mechanic. Mages can use Nimbus to clash with supernatural effects that would warp their mind, body or soul. Similarly, all other splats have some means of actively opposing supernatural effects. Active being the operative word here, and the reason for the change, since I find active countermeasures more rewarding to the players and less punishing than just saying &quot;nope, you don't beat his Withstand rating&quot;. It's also cooler to have supernaturals flashing their true nature when they start to butt heads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T09:21:23-07:00","id":887240,"title":"","content":"Yo. I got a few Merits in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits#post885111\">here</a> that might fit with your Mage hacks. <i>Especially</i> my take on Rote Mastery. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T13:49:42-07:00","id":887468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=887240#post887240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yo. I got a few Merits in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits#post885111\">here</a> that might fit with your Mage hacks. <i>Especially</i> my take on Rote Mastery. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct sir, <i>especially</i> your take on Rote Mastery. I tweaked it, as well as Page Master (great reference) and <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#heading=h.3n95kk2ar694\" target=\"_blank\">added them</a>, with proper attribution of course.<br /> <br /> Many thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-10-2016, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T17:16:48-07:00","id":887657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=887468#post887468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are correct sir, <i>especially</i> your take on Rote Mastery. I tweaked it, as well as Page Master (great reference) and <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#heading=h.3n95kk2ar694\" target=\"_blank\">added them</a>, with proper attribution of course.<br /> <br /> Many thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. And yeah. Page Master was really one of my favorite movies, plus it was very fitting for a name. Now for the Merit itself, I'm liking how you tied it to iterations of the Grimoire Merit. I might apply that to the original version as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T16:43:05-07:00","id":890242,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of allowing the use of Auras in Clash Of Wills, even though I have some doubts as to how it might work in practice. I also thought of a Paradigm Condition you might like. I just don't know if the description for gaining Beats is good enough. I came up with this one for patient masterminds that see the big picture, whether their modus operandi is Buddhist, Tzeentchian or anything in-between. The name is a reference to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metamorphic_rock\" target=\"_blank\"><b>metamorphic rocks</b></a>, which seemed more fitting than &quot;mercurial&quot; or &quot;protean&quot;.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Metamorphic</b></span></i><br /> <br /> You have seen the cycles of change that govern everything from beasts and men to empires and gods, and now you know the Truth. No one ever steps into the same river twice, the hero of today is the villain of tomorrow and life can come from ashes. To insist on permanence is futile, and to understand the movements of the cosmic wheel is paramount.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Moros or Thyrsus Awakening<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Beat:</b> You contribute to changing people and places with a focus on the long run, even if you have to disrupt their more immediate plans. This applies to yourself as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-13-2016, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T18:13:54-07:00","id":890309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=890242#post890242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the idea of allowing the use of Auras in Clash Of Wills, even though I have some doubts as to how it might work in practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also have some doubts, but those will have to be tested through play. The hope is that it'll give players a little more confidence and encourage indirect problem solving against obviously supernatural threats (like encouraging a Mind specialist to focus on controlling a Mummy's pawns, as opposed to direct domination of the Arisen himself).<br /> <br /> One thing I'm sure I'll need to add is a note that that Aura Clashing is to be used <b>in place</b> of any resistance roll you would receive. Otherwise it's punishing to non-mage contested powers, which already account for Supernal Advantage, and causes pointless roll inflation. Further drawbacks may be necessary, especially for Mages whom don't risk much by flaring their Nimbus. Maybe something like &quot;sleepers in your presence suffer from exposure to the competing supernatural effects, suffering a Breaking Point and counting as witnesses against all magic, even that which they cannot normally perceive, for the remainder of the scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Added the drawback. It definitely helps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=890242#post890242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also thought of a Paradigm Condition you might like. I just don't know if the description for gaining Beats is good enough. I came up with this one for patient masterminds that see the big picture, whether their modus operandi is Buddhist, Tzeentchian or anything in-between. The name is a reference to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metamorphic_rock\" target=\"_blank\"><b>metamorphic rocks</b></a>, which seemed more fitting than &quot;mercurial&quot; or &quot;protean&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Added it to the doc. Tweaked the Beat condition slightly to encourage such mages to deliberately cause conflict and undermine stability (which is, in their eyes, part of The Lie).<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-13-2016, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T18:42:18-07:00","id":890326,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you liked the Condition. I have some questions about Nimbus Clashing, however. What do you mean by &quot;a mage can only invoke their nimbus against a specific instance of a magical effect once&quot;? If a vampire tries to use Majesty on the mage and fails, but tries again within the same scene, can the mage Clash with their Nimbus once more? What if the vampire tried in another scene? What if the vampire tries Dominate instead of Majesty?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T19:30:22-07:00","id":890347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=890326#post890326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad you liked the Condition. I have some questions about Nimbus Clashing, however. What do you mean by &quot;a mage can only invoke their nimbus against a specific instance of a magical effect once&quot;? If a vampire tries to use Majesty on the mage and fails, but tries again within the same scene, can the mage Clash with their Nimbus once more? What if the vampire tried in another scene? What if the vampire tries Dominate instead of Majesty?</div> </div> </div> </div>Allow me to clarify the entire mechanic:<br /> <br /> A Mage can use his nimbus to Clash with any effect that would directly alter his mind, body or soul. Life to change his shape? Clash. Dominate to subjugate his mind? Clash. The heinous grip of a Beast threatens to seize his soul? Clash. A Mage, however, cannot Clash with effects that would harm him incidentally. For instance, he could not clash with a Life spell that created, then flung and infection at him. Nor could he Clash with a Uratha's supernaturally potent jaws, lightning slung by a Promethean or a Demon crippling his social assets. Put another way, if the effect would one-shot a character without recourse they can probably Clash with it, if it merely complicates their existence, affects them indirectly, or allows them some other form of defense (like Dodge, Soak, or Health) then it probably cannot be Clashed with. In the end it's a storyteller call.<br /> <br /> Now, when I say a Mage can only Clash with an effect once that means that, for each activation of a supernatural power the Mage may attempt to break it with his Nimbus only once. Taking Majesty as an example, if a Vampire attempted to tag a Mage with the Charmed condition that Mage could forgo his normal Contested roll and use his Nimbus to Clash. Should he fail, the Mage is Charmed, period. He cannot use his Nimbus to Clash again even if the scene or even the story (if the effect were longer) ends. However, if the Mage wins the Clash the Charmed Condition is resisted, the Vampire could attempt to Charm him again (though I'd consider that poor storytelling) and likewise the Mage could once more attempt to Clash.<br /> <br /> Now, on the topic of power spam. Personally I'd never have an NPC attempt the same approach twice in a scene and I'd prohibit a player from doing the same. However, as that runs into some weird scenarios across the games (For instance, does Clashing with <i>Dominate the Mind</i> prohibit all Mind powers? Just that spell? Justing Ruling Practices? What if the Mage devises an exceptionally similar spell? Etc.) I opted not to put that to rules. That is, IMO, the point where the storyteller and players must deem what is best for their tale.<br /> <br /> Is that more clear?<br /> <br /> Fundamentally the mechanic is there to offer players <b>some </b>recourse against effects that would otherwise rob them of all agency or do serious, irrevocable harm without affording them even the slightest roll. It's intended to achieve this in a dramatic manner, which conveys narratively that Mages (and full supernatural templates in general) are not to be trifled with and that the scene just got fucking serious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T20:37:10-07:00","id":890377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=890347#post890347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, when I say a Mage can only Clash with an effect once that means that, for each activation of a supernatural power the Mage may attempt to break it with his Nimbus only once. Taking Majesty as an example, if a Vampire attempted to tag a Mage with the Charmed condition that Mage could forgo his normal Contested roll and use his Nimbus to Clash. Should he fail, the Mage is Charmed, period. <u>He cannot use his Nimbus to Clash again even if the scene or even the story (if the effect were longer) ends.</u> However, if the Mage wins the Clash the Charmed Condition is resisted, the Vampire could attempt to Charm him again (though I'd consider that poor storytelling) and likewise the Mage could once more attempt to Clash.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Can he use his Nimbus against Majesty again after he Resolves the Charmed Condition (or any other Condition inflicted by Majesty after that one)? If he is trying to Resolve the Charmed Condition and another type of supernatural tries to control his emotions, can he still use his Nimbus?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=890347#post890347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, on the topic of power spam. Personally I'd never have an NPC attempt the same approach twice in a scene and I'd prohibit a player from doing the same. However, as that runs into some weird scenarios across the games (For instance, does Clashing with <i>Dominate the Mind</i> prohibit all Mind powers? Just that spell? Just Ruling Practices? What if the Mage devises an exceptionally similar spell? Etc.) I opted not to put that to rules. That is, IMO, the point where the storyteller and players must deem what is best for their tale.</div> </div> </div> </div> For simplicity's sake, I'd say that Clashing with &quot;Dominate The Mind&quot; protects you from all Mind spells. If you won the Clash against a Life spell meant to cripple your legs, you would also be protected from Life spells meant to turn you into a rat. This way, there will be no reason to bother with spamming powers, which in turn will encourage the use of different Arcana and tactics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T21:06:44-07:00","id":890391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=890377#post890377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Can he use his Nimbus against Majesty again after he Resolves the Charmed Condition (or any other Condition inflicted by Majesty after that one)? If he is trying to Resolve the Charmed Condition and another type of supernatural tries to control his emotions, can he still use his Nimbus?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. He cannot clash with that, specific instance of Charmed. A later instance, a different power, anything, is fair game. The point is to prohibit a player from attempting to Clash with the same effect over and over, and not prevent them from being able to Clash at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For simplicity's sake, I'd say that Clashing with &amp;quot;Dominate The Mind&amp;quot; protects you from all Mind spells. If you won the Clash against a Life spell meant to cripple your legs, you would also be protected from Life spells meant to turn you into a rat. This way, there will be no reason to bother with spamming powers, which in turn will encourage the use of different Arcana and tactics. </div> </div> </div>That's a fair ruling, hence why I left it to the Storyteller. I see no reason to rule further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T14:39:05-07:00","id":891377,"title":"","content":"I wrote a thing!<br /> <br /> It's a thing for Three Kingdoms of Darkness<br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Reach Heaven By Violence</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Core Power: If You Meet God...</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Keys</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: Stigmata Hearse</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dice Pool</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: Finesse + Weaponry</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Action</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Duration</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">It is easy to see why many cultures respect the sword, when death itself dwells at the edge of a blade. This power allows the Sin-Eater to reach any opponent with but a single step.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">:</span><br /> <br /> <i>Dramatic Failure</i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: The Sin-Eater very obviously disappears and reappears by the side of his opponent, but he may take no other actions that turn.</span><br /> <i>Failure</i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: For a short moment, the Sin-Eater seems to shimmer, but nothing else happens.</span><br /> <i>Success</i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: The Sin-Eater disappears in a cloud of ephemeral substance and appears at the side of a single opponent within sight and makes a reflexive attack.</span><br /> <i>Exceptional Success</i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: The attack is unexpected, and the opponent cannot apply Defence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Link 1: You Must Cut Him</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Keys</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: Phantasmal Curse</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Trigger</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: \u201cWhen the Sin-Eater makes a reflexive attack...\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">...They add their Power as additional damage modifier, once per scene as their weapon trails shadowy ephemera behind it in a single destructive cut. If this attack kills the target, the Sin-Eater's weapon becomes a Fetter with a single Numen and Key determined by the Storyteller and the Anchor of the Torn. This effect only lasts for a scene, however the Sin-Eater may spend a dot of Willpower to make it permanent.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T11:54:47-07:00","id":891901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=891377#post891377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote a thing!<br /> <br /> It's a thing for Three Kingdoms of Darkness<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't exactly put it in the doc, but I put something distinctly inspired by it, Deadly Shadows. A Manifestation about moving through, sensing through, and attacking through shadows. It's not quite the same as what you designed, but I think it accomplishes the same sort of horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T02:26:14-07:00","id":892390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=891901#post891901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't exactly put it in the doc, but I put something distinctly inspired by it, Deadly Shadows. A Manifestation about moving through, sensing through, and attacking through shadows. It's not quite the same as what you designed, but I think it accomplishes the same sort of horror.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's pretty cool.<br /> <br /> I've become rather enamoured with your system for Geist and will probably make a new thing regularily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T10:32:16-07:00","id":892610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=892390#post892390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's pretty cool.<br /> <br /> I've become rather enamoured with your system for Geist and will probably make a new thing regularily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woo! I love new thing, and I'm very glad my Geist hacks (e.g. Geister's Bizarre Adventure) are working for you.<br /> <br /> Actually, I have a bunch of other Manifestations I wrote up for different characters, I should probably add those to the doc.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>I totally forgot, I wrote up a second treatment of the Manifest Geister rules, much cleaner than my first. I'll post that here, and perhaps see about creating a more unified doc: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1chfmn9BlV5-xVLDfmTTR4DJdVwPdKSdG1AX8E1Xis94/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...8E1Xis94/edit#</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-17-2016, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T19:57:01-07:00","id":893821,"title":"","content":"I have a question about Aura Clashing for Beasts. Does the Lair Tilt used in the Clash have to be the opposite of what the other individual is using (e.g. Flooded against the Blast of a fire spirit)? That sounds like it would require a lot of interpretation and maybe end up looking like battles between Pok\u00e9mon Types. My intuition says a few of the official Lair Tilts can be applied in an Aura Clashing in more scenarios than the other Tilts, making the latter less desirable even if they fit a character's concept. Perhaps the Begotten could use their Horrors as Auras to &quot;scare away&quot; the opponent's power?<br /> <br /> I also noticed something about the Aura Clashing of Demons. You said they can switch between Covers or assume their full Demonic Forms to Clash. Demons have to spend 1 Aether and be both alone and unobserved to switch Covers, and assuming a full Demonic Form causes a compromise roll at -3. The first option would be unavailable per RAW since the opponent is observing the Demon, and the second option has its own risks. Perhaps the penalty to the compromise roll could be decreased if you are assuming your full Demonic Form for an Aura Clash?<br /> <br /> I made some observations about the adjustments that a Mage version of Bayonetta following your house rules would need. You don't have to reply to those if you don't want to.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I really like the &quot;Myth Of The Gun&quot; Mystic Art. It's perfect for Thyrsus!Bayonetta, along with Totemism. The problem with interpreting her as a Mage (aside from the usual Paradox/Quiescence/Dissonance) is that a big part of her charm lies in her over the top feats. She wouldn't be out of place in Exalted, and if she acted the same in the CoD, she would have very low Wisdom. Her magic style would have to be a lot more subtle, and she'd probably need some Inuring.<br /> <br /> Her relationship between Angels and Demons would have to be changed as well. I'd say that the Angels would be powerful and arrogant spirits operating as Balder's personal Choir that takes advantage of human beliefs. The Demons would be powerful spirits as well, but they'd be the purer, no-bullshit sort that can make deals but aren't anyone's slaves, which is why Thyrsus!Bayonetta likes them more. The exception would probably be Madame Butterfly, who sounds like a Supernal Patron and remains loyal to Bayonetta in the sequel.<br /> <br /> Even with all those alterations, Thyrsus!Bayonetta could still unleash some wild magic when she is inside the Shadow. Her quadruple guns are definitely Imbued and Enhanced, and her Wicked Weaves can be interpreted as her Nimbus + Imbued and Enhanced clothing. Her Gnosis would be 6 or 7. Her Arcana would be Life 4, Spirit 4, Time 3, Forces 3 and Matter 3. Her animal transformations and Witch Time would be her Praxes.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-18-2016, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T02:07:34-07:00","id":893911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=893821#post893821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about Aura Clashing for Beasts. Does the Lair Tilt used in the Clash have to be the opposite of what the other individual is using (e.g. Flooded against the Blast of a fire spirit)? That sounds like it would require a lot of interpretation and maybe end up looking like battles between Pok\u00e9mon Types. My intuition says a few of the official Lair Tilts can be applied in an Aura Clashing in more scenarios than the other Tilts, making the latter less desirable even if they fit a character's concept. Perhaps the Begotten could use their Horrors as Auras to &quot;scare away&quot; the opponent's power?<br /> <br /> I also noticed something about the Aura Clashing of Demons. You said they can switch between Covers or assume their full Demonic Forms to Clash. Demons have to spend 1 Aether and be both alone and unobserved to switch Covers, and assuming a full Demonic Form causes a compromise roll at -3. The first option would be unavailable per RAW since the opponent is observing the Demon, and the second option has its own risks. Perhaps the penalty to the compromise roll could be decreased if you are assuming your full Demonic Form for an Aura Clash?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're on point about Beasts and Demons. The intent for Demons was to give them a very potent, but somewhat conditional defense against pattern manipulation, but honestly it's too much book keeping. What I'll probably go for is this:<ul><li>Demons can Clash with effects that would warp their mind or body (their souls are inviolate, so no need there) by assuming Demonic Form. While in Demonic Form a demon is wholly immune to any effect that could be Clashed with, and immediately suppress any magics which were currently affecting their pattern while in Cover. This means that it is impossible to dominate, mutate, time-warp or otherwise muck up the pattern of a Demon in Demonic Form. This does not, however, apply to reprogramming by God-Machine infrastructure, or the reality bending powers of Rank 6+ beings.</li> </ul>That accomplishes more cleanly and absolutely the desired effect; to make Demons fucking horrifying for other splats, and render Demonic Form the power house it is intended to be. As for Beast, I went with Tilts off the top of my head, but you're right, they don't work. Though, I should take a moment to note that when I envision clashing it's not summoning waves to snuff fire, indeed the Blast Numen would not be something I'd allow a Clash against, it already has it's limits. It's more the supernatural being flaring their base nature and rejecting powers that would change it. The Beast briefly unveiling their horror in an Anima Flare/American Gods, dual presence sort of way works well. It'll need a drawback, like causing heroes to hone in on the Beast when used, or greatly increasing the chances of witnesses becoming heroes. Actually, both of those are probably sufficient.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, let me brainstorm a bit. Your thoughts are welcome:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u><b>Vampire - Predatory Aura</b></u><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Effect</b>: Clash with effect. If successful inflict one of three Vampiric conditions on your target.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Risk Frenzy</div><u><b>Werewolf - Shifting Up</b></u><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Effect</b>: Shift up one step towards Gauru, Clash with effect. If in Gauru add +2 to the Clash roll. Werewolves auto Clash with all Clashable effects while in Gauru.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Shifting up inflicts lunacy on bystanders. If in Gauru, risk Kuruth.</div><b><u>Mage - Nimbus Flare</u></b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Effect</b>: Clash with effect. If successful inflict your Nimbus Tilt(s)<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Sleeper bystanders suffer a breaking point and count as witnesses for the rest of the scene.</div><u><b>Promethean - Kindling</b></u><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Effect</b>: Unveil your disfigurements, Clash with effect.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Intensify disquiet in all those present.</div><u><b>Changeling - Dropping the Mask</b></u><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Effect</b>: Drop the mask, Clash with effect.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Everyone can see you for what you are, Huntsmen and Gentry can feel the mask fall.</div><u><b>Sin-Eater - Manifest Geister</b></u><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Effect</b>: Manifest your Geist, Clash with effect.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: ??? (I've got nothing, Synergy risk?)</div><u><b>Mummy - Sybaris</b></u><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Effect</b>: Unleash Terror Sybaris, Clash with effect.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Mortals nearby suffer breaking points, everyone is afraid of you, you look like a corpse.</div><u><b>Demon - Demonic Form</b></u><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Effect: </b>Assume Demonic form, become immune to pattern manipulation while in Demonic form.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Suffer compromise.</div><u><b>Beast - Unveil Horror</b></u><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Effect: </b>Reveal your horror briefly, Clash with effect. If successful, and in a resonant location, you may invoke a Lair Tilt.<br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Heroes are drawn to your location. If there are no heroes to hunt you, the probability of a bystander becoming a hero increases exponentially.</div>Note: These are not supposed to be perfectly balanced against one another. Mummies have very few drawbacks, Demons have a huge drawback but by far the strongest option, etc.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Edit: </b>I'm trying to find a proper wording to convey succinctly when a Clash is appropriate. Currently I'm going by &quot;when the storyteller deems it&quot;, but that just doesn't feel clear enough. Currently I'm toying with:<ul><li>A supernatural being can Clash with an effect when that effect would directly subvert the very essence of their being or personality. For instance, if a Mage attempts to light a changeling's bone marrow on fire that changeling could Clash as his bones being on fire would be a clear subversion of his essential being. However, that same changeling could not clash if the mage manipulated the ambient air to cause him to burst into flame, burning when exposed to great heat is perfectly natural. Similarly, a demon in demonic form would be immune to being personally, singularly frozen in time, but could not respond if the Mage stopped local time altogether in the area. Again, a demon being locked out of time while everything else moves is unnatural, but not moving because <b>nothing </b>is moving, well that's perfectly normal.</li> </ul>I'm still not perfectly happy with the wording, but I think it gets the point across better than my current pitch. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=893821#post893821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made some observations about the adjustments that a Mage version of Bayonetta following your house rules would need. You don't have to reply to those if you don't want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd reply, but there's not much else to say. Though, you are right that Bayonetta is a tad silly for CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-19-2016, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T02:54:09-07:00","id":893923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=892610#post892610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woo! I love new thing, and I'm very glad my Geist hacks (e.g. Geister's Bizarre Adventure) are working for you.<br /> <br /> Actually, I have a bunch of other Manifestations I wrote up for different characters, I should probably add those to the doc.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>I totally forgot, I wrote up a second treatment of the Manifest Geister rules, much cleaner than my first. I'll post that here, and perhaps see about creating a more unified doc: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1chfmn9BlV5-xVLDfmTTR4DJdVwPdKSdG1AX8E1Xis94/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...8E1Xis94/edit#</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is really cool, but could you please clarify the Soul-Glass and Martial Keys and what they do?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T10:18:47-07:00","id":894138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=893923#post893923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is really cool, but could you please clarify the Soul-Glass and Martial Keys and what they do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, forgot to note those:<ul><li><b>Soulglass </b>was devised by Metamurpho (one of my players). I<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">t involves art, mimicry, and living souls. T</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">hings like trapping people's souls in mirrors, having art stare into your </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">soul, </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">becoming a simulacre of someone's thoughts. T</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">hink about how primitive people thought mirrors entrapped your </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">soul</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> and go from there. Sample Manifestations might include using The Caul to become someone's doppleganger, Oracle to gaze through reflective surfaces, or the Curse to inflict soulessness.</span></span></li> <li><b>Martial </b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">was my own, it deals in weapons, warfare, tactics and battlefields. Things like inciting armed conflict, making weapons more/less lethal, or giving someone PTSD. Think about the hectic, hellish experience of being on the battlefield and you're on the right track. Sample Manifestations might include using the Shroud to become immune to weaponry and firearms, the Hearse to turn a car into a tank, or Boneyard to place and entire area under suppressing fire.</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u200bAlso, it's worthwhile to note that I run Geist under the assumption that more, custom keys exist, and that those given in the book are merely examples not the be all and end all of ghostly themes.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:09:52-07:00","id":894306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=894138#post894138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, forgot to note those:<ul><li><b>Soulglass </b>was devised by Metamurpho (one of my players). I<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">t involves art, mimicry, and living souls. T</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">hings like trapping people's souls in mirrors, having art stare into your </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">soul, </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">becoming a simulacre of someone's thoughts. T</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">hink about how primitive people thought mirrors entrapped your </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">soul</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> and go from there. Sample Manifestations might include using The Caul to become someone's doppleganger, Oracle to gaze through reflective surfaces, or the Curse to inflict soulessness.</span></span></li> <li><b>Martial </b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">was my own, it deals in weapons, warfare, tactics and battlefields. Things like inciting armed conflict, making weapons more/less lethal, or giving someone PTSD. Think about the hectic, hellish experience of being on the battlefield and you're on the right track. Sample Manifestations might include using the Shroud to become immune to weaponry and firearms, the Hearse to turn a car into a tank, or Boneyard to place and entire area under suppressing fire.</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u200bAlso, it's worthwhile to note that I run Geist under the assumption that more, custom keys exist, and that those given in the book are merely examples not the be all and end all of ghostly themes.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's pretty cool, I am already in love with Martial so I'll get lots of mileage out of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:55:37-07:00","id":896160,"title":"","content":"I ended up working out a Curse for a Proximi line while working out some of the Mage 2E House Rules I'm putting together. Whatcha think? <hr /><br /> <b>Abyssal Bane</b><br /> The Quartermaines were notable for their skill in manipulating Mana and various forms of mystical energy. Conversely, they suffer gravely in the presence of any Abyssal entities and phenomena. Mages of Quartermaine blood suffer the Disoriented Condition as a persistent effect whenever they are within sensory range of an Abyssal Intruder or Verge, or an active Paradox Condition. When rolling their Wisdom to contain Paradox as backlash under such conditions, they lose the 10-again quality, subtract 1s from successes, and treat all failures as Dramatic Failures.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Quartermaine Proximi<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> None<br /> <b>Beat:</b> You suffer Paradox as a result of the Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:22:43-07:00","id":897114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=896160#post896160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ended up working out a Curse for a Proximi line while working out some of the Mage 2E House Rules I'm putting together. Whatcha think? <hr /><br /> <b>Abyssal Bane</b><br /> The Quartermaines were notable for their skill in manipulating Mana and various forms of mystical energy. Conversely, they suffer gravely in the presence of any Abyssal entities and phenomena. Mages of Quartermaine blood suffer the Disoriented Condition as a persistent effect whenever they are within sensory range of an Abyssal Intruder or Verge, or an active Paradox Condition. When rolling their Wisdom to contain Paradox as backlash under such conditions, they lose the 10-again quality, subtract 1s from successes, and treat all failures as Dramatic Failures.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Quartermaine Proximi<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> None<br /> <b>Beat:</b> You suffer Paradox as a result of the Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. In fact I added it to the doc, with only the slightest tweak in Beat management.<br /> <br /> I gather the Quartermaines specialized in fuel stats, like Mana, Essence and Plasm? Any chance of an Art, or perhaps I should write one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T18:39:06-07:00","id":897416,"title":"","content":"Yep. They did. And I think your tweak to the Curse's Beat is much better.<br /> <br /> I got no ideas on how to write them up as an Art, sadly. I'm going with a few different interpretations for Proximi in addition to using (most of) the core material, although I might use your concepts for Arts as the basis for Proximi-exclusive Attainments/Merits. But if you plan on writing them out as an Art, then focusing on their specialty in fuel stats <i>is</i> a good place to start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T19:46:09-07:00","id":897485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=897416#post897416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. They did. And I think your tweak to the Curse's Beat is much better.<br /> <br /> I got no ideas on how to write them up as an Art, sadly. I'm going with a few different interpretations for Proximi in addition to using (most of) the core material, although I might use your concepts for Arts as the basis for Proximi-exclusive Attainments/Merits. But if you plan on writing them out as an Art, then focusing on their specialty in fuel stats <i>is</i> a good place to start.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem, I figured as much. <br /> <br /> The first thought that came to mind was an Art based around power. Steam power, water power, electrical power. Experimenting with Yantra that fuel as a means of channelling esoteric power sources. Maybe give the Art a Da Vinci or Tesla feel, Sons of Aether to use an Ascension example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T22:28:37-07:00","id":897580,"title":"","content":"Hey, sorry for the delayed answer. Your new suggestions for the effects and drawbacks of each splat's Aura sound interesting. I know you said that they aren't supposed to be balanced, but giving universal immunity to Demons in their true forms is crazy useful, even with the caveat of compromise and still being vulnerable to Infrastructure and godlike entities.<br /> <br /> I would add that they are still vulnerable to the following: each other's Embeds/Exploits/Gadgets, the powers of certain Cryptids/Stigmatics/Offspring/Nephilim and all Angelic powers. This way, the most effective way to get rid of Demons is to instigate betrayal among them (which I imagine isn't very hard) and helping out an Angel in exchange for the use of its powers and Cult. This maintains the gameplay of espionage. As you've said, indirect powers still work fine against them (e.g. an aimed Forces spell, a changeling's punch enhanced with Stone Contracts).<br /> <br /> I want to add that Demons could also be vulnerable to the powers and natural weaponry of the denizens of the Invisible Realms, due to the G-M having less protections against those phenomena. This means that changelings can ask hobgoblins and <u><b>maybe</b></u> the Gentry for help, werewolves can call upon their Totems, Mages can spy on them through Familiars or summon Supernal entities, and Sin-Eaters and Mummies can pull up all sorts of ghoulies from the Underworld. At the ST's discretion, the magic items related to the Invisible Realms can work on Demons in their true forms if the items' methods are indirect enough.<br /> <br /> Prometheans and Vampires usually lack those kinds of allies and items, unfortunately. If you feel comfortable with implying some relationship between Aether and Pyros (not the same as &quot;God-Machine = Principle&quot;, mind you), you can let Transmutations like Electrification and Vulcanus be exceptions to the universal immunity of full Demonic Forms. I'm really unsure about this one, as we have few 2ED spoilers for Promethean. What do you think about <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gfFNSeOv-xvhM1cC6h9Zfpyt11XcmIUvtCjbgSmYWgg/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#heading=h.4sijm5g3prcx\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sanguine Craft</b></a>?<br /> <br /> As a last note, I'd say that one of the results of failing a Compromise roll triggered by Aura Clashing could be a forced Burned Condition (i.e. stuck in full Demonic Form drawing attention with their appearance and Aetheric Resonance) with a duration proportional to Primum.<br /> <br /> I am not sure of how to phrase what circumstances allow an Aura Clash. I'll tell you if I think of a concise and clear definition.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For Sin-Eaters, using their Geister in Aura Clashes could attract the attention of ghosts and those with ghost-sense (e.g. a Moros). It could also result in opening or locking Avernian Gates within a radius proportional to Psyche. I would not make any of that an automatic risk to Synergy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-24-2016, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T02:00:10-07:00","id":897641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=897485#post897485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No problem, I figured as much.<br /> <br /> The first thought that came to mind was an Art based around power. Steam power, water power, electrical power. Experimenting with Yantra that fuel as a means of channelling esoteric power sources. Maybe give the Art a Da Vinci or Tesla feel, Sons of Aether to use an Ascension example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Giving the Quartermaines a scientific bent to their magical style (a la Sons of Aether) does make sense, though I was also open to the idea of them dealing with magical items of various stripes (Imbued Items, Fetishes, Relics, etc.). Especially since the one named Quartermaine Proximus I conceptualized happens to collect and keep a personal vault of such objects. That said, maybe they could have both an academic <i>and</i> a scientific theme to them. Which could go well with their (former, in my universe) association with the Silver Ladder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:17:57-07:00","id":898070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=897641#post897641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Giving the Quartermaines a scientific bent to their magical style (a la Sons of Aether) does make sense, though I was also open to the idea of them dealing with magical items of various stripes (Imbued Items, Fetishes, Relics, etc.). Especially since the one named Quartermaine Proximus I conceptualized happens to collect and keep a personal vault of such objects. That said, maybe they could have both an academic <i>and</i> a scientific theme to them. Which could go well with their (former, in my universe) association with the Silver Ladder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind describing your Quartermaines? I basically just went with the first inspiration that hit me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:37:42-07:00","id":898097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=897580#post897580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, sorry for the delayed answer. Your new suggestions for the effects and drawbacks of each splat's Aura sound interesting. I know you said that they aren't supposed to be balanced, but giving universal immunity to Demons in their true forms is crazy useful, even with the caveat of compromise and still being vulnerable to Infrastructure and godlike entities.<br /> <br /> I would add that they are still vulnerable to the following: each other's Embeds/Exploits/Gadgets, the powers of certain Cryptids/Stigmatics/Offspring/Nephilim and all Angelic powers. This way, the most effective way to get rid of Demons is to instigate betrayal among them (which I imagine isn't very hard) and helping out an Angel in exchange for the use of its powers and Cult. This maintains the gameplay of espionage. As you've said, indirect powers still work fine against them (e.g. an aimed Forces spell, a changeling's punch enhanced with Stone Contracts).<br /> <br /> I want to add that Demons could also be vulnerable to the powers and natural weaponry of the denizens of the Invisible Realms, due to the G-M having less protections against those phenomena. This means that changelings can ask hobgoblins and <u><b>maybe</b></u> the Gentry for help, werewolves can call upon their Totems, Mages can spy on them through Familiars or summon Supernal entities, and Sin-Eaters and Mummies can pull up all sorts of ghoulies from the Underworld. At the ST's discretion, the magic items related to the Invisible Realms can work on Demons in their true forms if the items' methods are indirect enough.<br /> <br /> Prometheans and Vampires usually lack those kinds of allies and items, unfortunately. If you feel comfortable with implying some relationship between Aether and Pyros (not the same as &quot;God-Machine = Principle&quot;, mind you), you can let Transmutations like Electrification and Vulcanus be exceptions to the universal immunity of full Demonic Forms. I'm really unsure about this one, as we have few 2ED spoilers for Promethean. What do you think about <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gfFNSeOv-xvhM1cC6h9Zfpyt11XcmIUvtCjbgSmYWgg/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#heading=h.4sijm5g3prcx\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sanguine Craft</b></a>?<br /> <br /> As a last note, I'd say that one of the results of failing a Compromise roll triggered by Aura Clashing could be a forced Burned Condition (i.e. stuck in full Demonic Form drawing attention with their appearance and Aetheric Resonance) with a duration proportional to Primum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, going through the list of Embeds and Exploits there are actually very few that Demonic Form would be immune to. The same can be said of Electrification and Vulcanis (which, as of 1e, have nothing I'd give a Demon a Clash for). Mostly what they end up with is immunity to mind control, instant death or disability, and the most unpleasant combat debuffs (like Hesitate). All that comes at the cost of serious compromise, the sort that marks the end of any hope for subtlety or espionage. The real limiting factor is story, since I generally assume that Demons will have some narrative reason for not wanting their nature to be known.<br /> <br /> So for now I think I'll stick with it as written, at least until I can give it a proper playtest (which could be a while). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=897580#post897580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure of how to phrase what circumstances allow an Aura Clash. I'll tell you if I think of a concise and clear definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I added one to the docs. I think it's as good as I'm likely to get.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=897580#post897580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: For Sin-Eaters, using their Geister in Aura Clashes could attract the attention of ghosts and those with ghost-sense (e.g. a Moros). It could also result in opening or locking Avernian Gates within a radius proportional to Psyche. I would not make any of that an automatic risk to Synergy.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm thinking now, after a brainstorm with Metamurpho, is that Sin-Eaters don't quite get a standard &quot;counterspell&quot; sort of Clash. Instead, even if they are charmed or disabled their Geist retains its will and can Manifest to defend the Sin-Eater even while inert. Of course that'd only works with my Geist hack, but hey, they're my docs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T16:39:47-07:00","id":898366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=898070#post898070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind describing your Quartermaines? I basically just went with the first inspiration that hit me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Formerly affiliated with the Silver Ladder, the Quartermaines are a Proximi Dynasty who have also been blessed with an abundance of Sleepwalkers across generations. They specialized in magic that dealt in the manipulation of Mana and various other esoteric energies. This also translated to a predilection for mastering control over the more mundane energies of the world, as well as an affinity for Imbued Items, Supernal Artifacts, and other supernatural relics.<br /> <br /> <b>Rotes:</b> The Quartermaines approach their magic from either an academic or scientific stance. And most of their rotes deal in the direct manipulation of mundane or supernatural energies. Many family members also demonstrate a preference for investing Supernal power into Imbued Items, and hold interest in similar objects such as spirit-based fetishes and the mementos of Sin-Eaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-24-2016, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:37:21-07:00","id":900535,"title":"","content":"I noticed something confusing in the fourth benefit of Prelacy. It says that True Fae will allow you to summon Huntsmen, but the latter need to fulfill the Approaches set by changelings to regain their Yearning points (and they can only hold up to 10). They are very cunning and have no mercy, sure, but it seems like they'll only be used for one scene. They do start with 6 Yearning, so it's possible that a Mage who phrases his request just right can get precisely what he asked for. I believe the list of beings you can summon should include hobgoblins, loyalist changelings/fetches and other thinking constructs of dreamstuff the True Fae might have stored away. If a Mage needs the direct help of a True Fae, he should pay a heavy price and be ready for his words to be twisted deliberately or not.<br /> <br /> I know that the beings cited in the fourth benefit do not constitute an exhaustive list. It was just an observation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:40:05-07:00","id":900536,"title":"","content":"I also remembered a house rule you once applied to Quiescence. If a Sleeper loses a dot of Integrity due to witnessing Supernal and/or Abyssal phenomena, he can take a Persistent Condition to remember all those phenomena they witnessed in the scene. Should they regain the dot associated with that Condition, it is Resolved, but the memories of Supernal/Abyssal phenomena also go away.<br /> <br /> With this house rule, Sleepers can investigate Mage-related events further, but their sanity still erodes as they go deeper and deeper, Arkham Horror-style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-26-2016, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T08:33:56-07:00","id":903566,"title":"","content":"Got <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=903289#post903289\">another Merit</a> you might be interested in adding. Especially since it fits very well for the Tsuchimikado Proximi and their association with spirits and the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T12:49:39-07:00","id":905113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=898366#post898366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Formerly affiliated with the Silver Ladder, the Quartermaines are a Proximi Dynasty who have also been blessed with an abundance of Sleepwalkers across generations. They specialized in magic that dealt in the manipulation of Mana and various other esoteric energies. This also translated to a predilection for mastering control over the more mundane energies of the world, as well as an affinity for Imbued Items, Supernal Artifacts, and other supernatural relics.<br /> <br /> <b>Rotes:</b> The Quartermaines approach their magic from either an academic or scientific stance. And most of their rotes deal in the direct manipulation of mundane or supernatural energies. Many family members also demonstrate a preference for investing Supernal power into Imbued Items, and hold interest in similar objects such as spirit-based fetishes and the mementos of Sin-Eaters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I think I'll stick with the scientific focus, for my purposes it aligns well thematically and fills a whole in my own setting. Just FYI I've got them placed as a high standing group within the Mysterium, obsessed with understanding the nature of mana. I may, at some later point, write a few Rotes for them even. <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=898366#post898366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=903289#post903289\">another Merit</a> you might be interested in adding. Especially since it fits very well for the Tsuchimikado Proximi and their association with spirits and the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tweaked. Added.</span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T12:57:19-07:00","id":905117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=900535#post900535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed something confusing in the fourth benefit of Prelacy. It says that True Fae will allow you to summon Huntsmen, but the latter need to fulfill the Approaches set by changelings to regain their Yearning points (and they can only hold up to 10). They are very cunning and have no mercy, sure, but it seems like they'll only be used for one scene. They do start with 6 Yearning, so it's possible that a Mage who phrases his request just right can get precisely what he asked for. I believe the list of beings you can summon should include hobgoblins, loyalist changelings/fetches and other thinking constructs of dreamstuff the True Fae might have stored away. If a Mage needs the direct help of a True Fae, he should pay a heavy price and be ready for his words to be twisted deliberately or not.<br /> <br /> I know that the beings cited in the fourth benefit do not constitute an exhaustive list. It was just an observation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that wasn't exactly written with Changeling 2e rules wholly in mind. You are right in reading that the list is not exhaustive, I'd also point out that anyone with 4 dots of Prelacy is in deep with their patron power. That's top cultist/right hand man territory so I deemed it appropriate that such characters have access to some of their patron's greatest assets. Naturally abuse of that privilege will see repercussions appropriate to the patron. Plus, it's not like the being is compelled to serve the Mage, just like Supernal Summoning all that's done is they are brought to him. From there he'll have to leverage further magic, or his patron's favor, to make them obey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=900536#post900536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also remembered a house rule you once applied to Quiescence. If a Sleeper loses a dot of Integrity due to witnessing Supernal and/or Abyssal phenomena, he can take a Persistent Condition to remember all those phenomena they witnessed in the scene. Should they regain the dot associated with that Condition, it is Resolved, but the memories of Supernal/Abyssal phenomena also go away.<br /> <br /> With this house rule, Sleepers can investigate Mage-related events further, but their sanity still erodes as they go deeper and deeper, Arkham Horror-style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right! I'd forgotten that one, I'll get it into the doc. Thanks for the reminder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:45:56-07:00","id":923390,"title":"","content":"Your house rules for Aura Clashing are inspiring me to create a Hack for True Names. Each splat would have a different means to protect their True Name, and would suffer distinct drawbacks when someone uses it against them. This is meant to prevent mind readers and such from easily discovering True Names and enslaving other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Here are my vague ideas so far. What do you think? If you're interested, please send me a PM so we can discuss this further.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf:</b> You may ask your Pack Totem to protect all the True Names of the pack. The Totem treats their protection as a Ban, but should you lose their favor somehow, your True Names will be vulnerable for a full lunar cycle (28 days). Certain spirits with the Binding Vow Numen may try to rope the pack into deals that use their True Names. Ghost Wolves can ask the Totem for this protection too.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage:</b> Your True Name is securely locked within the Watchtower you signed. To discover it, others must enter your Oneiros and navigate the part that represents how you remember your Mystery Play and the Watchtower. This area will be protected by Supernal entities linked to your Path, Abyssals if you're a Scelestus and maybe Ochemata/Royal Avatars if you're a Seer with enough Prelacy. Certain Merits and Attainments can make this navigation easier.<br /> <br /> <b>Demon: </b>You treat your angelic designation as a True Name, which is cut off from the G-M's databanks when you Fall. You may discover a Demon's True Name by investigating one or more of their Covers until they unravel from Compromise rolls. The Demon may attempt to buy back this information from you via a Pact only (no mind control or memory wiping powers, but everything else is fair game).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T10:54:35-07:00","id":932967,"title":"","content":"I stumbled on your homebrew thread while looking for inspiration on how to convert the Persona video game series (by Atlus, and a spin-off of their even larger Shin Megami Tensei RPG series), and your approach at converting Geist for Second Edition is seriously what I've been looking for. The way you give the Geist their own stats, the capacity of acting independently from their Sin-Eater, and how customization they are to the player's intended fighting style is beyond perfect.<br /> <br /> I was wondering if I could have your permission to use your Geist material as a basis for my attempt at making a Persona: the Blatant Fanboy Pandering fansplat? For the moment it's one of those &quot;only for my gaming group&quot; type things, so I don't know if I would &quot;publish&quot; it online, but whether or not I make it a public project, full credit would obviously be given to you, with plenty of links to your original thread and google docs, to make sure people checkout your work.<br /> <br /> Regardless, yo uare doing excellent work, keep it up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7951-taroh","name":"Taroh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T18:09:22-07:00","id":933669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taroh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=932967#post932967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I stumbled on your homebrew thread while looking for inspiration on how to convert the Persona video game series (by Atlus, and a spin-off of their even larger Shin Megami Tensei RPG series), and your approach at converting Geist for Second Edition is seriously what I've been looking for. The way you give the Geist their own stats, the capacity of acting independently from their Sin-Eater, and how customization they are to the player's intended fighting style is beyond perfect.<br /> <br /> I was wondering if I could have your permission to use your Geist material as a basis for my attempt at making a Persona: the Blatant Fanboy Pandering fansplat? For the moment it's one of those &quot;only for my gaming group&quot; type things, so I don't know if I would &quot;publish&quot; it online, but whether or not I make it a public project, full credit would obviously be given to you, with plenty of links to your original thread and google docs, to make sure people checkout your work.<br /> <br /> Regardless, yo uare doing excellent work, keep it up!</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course you can use it, that's why its public. Attribution is all I request.<br /> <br /> Persona was actually one of the inspirations for the hack, the other (larger) source being Jojo's Bizarre Adventure. Though, fair warning, the hack does require a lot of cooperation between ST and player to make the Manifestation system work to its fullest. But you are clearly alright with large scale homebrew so that should be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T05:07:20-07:00","id":935001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=933669#post933669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course you can use it, that's why its public. Attribution is all I request.<br /> <br /> Persona was actually one of the inspirations for the hack, the other (larger) source being Jojo's Bizarre Adventure. Though, fair warning, the hack does require a lot of cooperation between ST and player to make the Manifestation system work to its fullest. But you are clearly alright with large scale homebrew so that should be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Greatly appreciate, it, thank you! And Jojo's Bizarre Adventure is a series I've been meaning to look into for a while, it's kind of a funny coincidence that you mention it as helping you flesh out your Geist Hack.<br /> <br /> And yeah, The Manifestation system is definitly what I will spend the most time on seeing if I can keep it as is or modify. My original intention before finding your hack was to just have a typical 5 dot power progression thing akin to Disciplines for Vampires, but that's still 22 different power sets to develop and balance out somehow. Regardless, this is a thread about your homebrew hacks, not my lukewarm attempts at doing the same, so I'll just leave it at that, and thank you again. I will notify you you if I ever publish any of my work, so you can confirm that I give you credit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7951-taroh","name":"Taroh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T22:26:30-07:00","id":966062,"title":"","content":"I'll take a shot at drafting up a Geist: the Sin-Eaters Keychain although it's ended up as a doozy.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">GHOSTLY DETECTIVE\u2019S PHANTOM TRICKS</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Core Manifestation: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Enter the Ghost World</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stillness Boneyard</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No roll</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Plasm</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: as long as the Sin-Eater wishes, and then time returns to normal</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sin-Eater pauses time by entering a potent state of Twilight. They may bring along a number of individuals nearby that do not exceed the Sin-Eater\u2019s Willpower score, although ghosts and those who have died at least once do not count towards this limit. The Sin-Eater and companions can converse freely or tackle purely Mental challenges while time is paused. However they cannot leave the current location (within Psyche * 10 yards) of where the Sin-Eater activated this ability, nor can they impact the environment in any way. When this ability ends time resumes and everyone is where they were when time was paused. Other Supernaturals may be aware a supernatural ability took place but learning what happened during paused time would be difficult. Prolonged delay of the present, however, may trigger Breaking Point type rolls at Storyteller discretion.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Link #1: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>4 Minutes to Death</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stygian Oracle</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trigger: \u201cEnter the Ghost World was used in range of a corpse that died in the last 4 hours.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sin-Eater (plus any companions) observes the last four minutes the corpse was alive. The Sin Eater can rewind, fast forward or pause time during these last four minutes (the same as Enter the Ghost World). The Sin-Eater and companions do not exist in the events of the past (not even the Twilight of the past) although they are not obstructed by physical matter and can pass anywhere within range, centered on the \u2018living\u2019 corpse. Thus information outside of the victim\u2019s perspective could be learned. Ending this ability returns the party to the present.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Link #2: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Mortal Recall</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Passion Oracle</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trigger: \u201cThe Sin-Eater activates 4 Minutes to Death\u2026\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sin-Eater may beckon the ghost of the departed victim into their Ghost World if they wish, either from the Underworld or wherever they were when Enter the Ghost World was activated. This does not endear the ghost to the Sin-Eater or compell them to answer in any way. Storyteller discretion is used on how much the ghost can remember/is willing to share about the events of their death and their life. A recent ghost may have trouble recalling their death or a despondent one may be adverse with the Sin-Eater tangling with their death. A traumatic death may result in a non-cognizant ghost. Someone who has accepted their death (or is tangled in other complications) may have already moved on and thus would not be available for the summons.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Link #3: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Tricking Out Time</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stygian Marionette (or Stygian Boneyard)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trigger: \u201cThe Sin-Eater has observed 4 Minutes to Death once AND spends 1 Plasm\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sin-Eater channels an additional Plasm into their revisit of the victim\u2019s last 4 minutes alive. The Sin-Eater cannot affect other characters nor be heard by them but they can subtlety manipulate the environment of the past to see what changes, although when they return to the present the victim is still dead. Only physical actions can influence the past, requiring either Strength (Power) or Dexterity (Finesse) plus a suitable Skill.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Link #4: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Kismet Switch</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cold-Wind Marionette</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trigger: \u201cTime was paused while another object was in motion OR Tricking Out Time was activated.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Before time is unpaused, the Sin-Eater is able to switch an object in motion with a proportionately similar object based on profile or shape. A bullet could be replaced with a carrot or ice cream cone, a speeding car with a toy car, a manhole cover with a dinner plate or other such associations, provided the objects are present in the scene. The inertia and placement of the switched objects holds true for the previous conditions in the scene: an objected swapped into a moving path will gain that momentum, and an object moved to an inert location will remain so, although once time flows again natural physics will take its course. The Sin-Eater can move an object of a Size within their Size + Strength + Science.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Link #5: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Tune In, Drop Out</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stillness Dirge or Stillness Oracle</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trigger: \u201cThe Sin-Eater encounters a former companion from Enter the Ghost World.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once per scene, when within range of a former companion that has entered the \u2018Ghost World\u2019 the Sin-Eater is able to communicate with them outside of time. Treat this as a free use of Enter the Ghost World once per scene. However, linked manifestations are not possible. The Sin Eater would have to activate \u2018Enter the Ghost World\u2019 with its usual cost to use linked manifestations. The Sin-Eater can invalidate a target from Tune In Drop Out at any time they wish.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Link #6: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>More Distance Past</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Industrial Hearse (or Industrial Oracle)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trigger: \u201cA communications call is made during 4 Minutes to Death.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sin-Eater focuses on a phone call or similar communication between devices during 4 Minutes to Death. The Sin-Eater can clearly hear what occurred during the call. If the call is via a landline connection the Sin Eater can transport themselves to the other receiver instantly as they explore the past. They are still limited to the amount of time left in 4 Minutes to Death after the call begins. When exploring the new location the range is centered on the receiver at arrival.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Link #7: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Fate Aversion</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stigmata Marionette</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trigger: \u201cThe victim in 4 Minutes to Death has a preventable death.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Preventable death means the environment can be manipulated to keep the victim alive. The victim succumbing to old age or illness is not preventable. Knocking away a killer\u2019s weapon, getting the victim needed medical attention, or stopping a disaster before it happened are all viable means to prevent death. The Sin-Eater may use other applicable linked manifestations as needed. To overwrite the past and restore the victim to life, however, requires 2 Plasm and the Sin Eater completing an extended action with a threshold of amount of damage the victim received during the killing blow, rolling Psyche + 1.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The rescued victim briefly passes through the Ghost World upon being restored to life. The Sin-Eater reappears where they were when Enter the Ghost World was triggered, with the restored mortal appearing wherever at Storyteller discretion. Only the Sin-Eater, victim and any Ghost World companions will recognize that the past was changed as they return to a new present.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Link #8: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Fated Death</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stygian Pit (or Stygian Rage)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trigger: \u201cIn saving a victim from past fate, the one who had a hand in their death becomes a valid target.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is far easier to keep Death\u2019s books (that a death still occurred in the past) than undo a death completely. The Sin-Eater declares a way for the person who participated in the death of the victim to die themselves, either via the same method or another option available in the scene. The Sin-Eater must pay 2 Plasm and complete an extended action using Strength or Dexterity, an applicable Skill and their Psyche, with a threshold of the target\u2019s Willpower score and Supernatural Advantage. If the Sin-Eater is successful the new target dies, their soul/ghost immediately dragged off into the Underworld. The death of this victim can impact the return to the present in varied ways determined by the Storyteller. Only the Sin-Eater, Ghost World companions and the newly dead target will recognize that the past was changed as they return to a new present.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Link #9: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Outrace the Clock</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stygian Hearse</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trigger: \u201cDuring 4 Minutes to Death another corpse that died with 4 hours of that time is discovered in range.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By focusing solely on the past portrayed in 4 Minutes to Death it allows the Sin-Eater to race backwards from the present they paused. The Sin-Eater may chose to visit the 4 Minutes to Death of this newly discovered corpse, although they must immediately make a Synergy check with a penalty equal to the number of linked manifestations used since activating Enter the Ghost World. On a failure not only is Synergy lost but the Sin-Eater is booted back to the present they paused, unable to enact 4 Minutes to Death on the first corpse ever again. On a success the Sin-Eater can view the new victim\u2019s 4 Minutes to Death as usual.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Keychain idea is really awesome for something to use until Geist gets its 2E revisions. It fits the means along newer game lines for customizing the powers presented in the books, such as Interlocks for Demons and Nightmares for Beasts. I plan to use this when introducing Geists and Sin-Eaters into my crossover game when ghostly antics become more important to the plot.<br /> <br /> Although when not basing a Keychain off of my favorite DS game I admit I'm not as great at determining what the core manifestation should be to build other powers off of. I have numerous ideas for keychains but I'll keep the next idea simple for now.<br /> <br /> I'm working on a Stricken Gatekeeper NPC who is an urban photographer getting some notice in the art scene. She died from prolonged asbestos exposure in her crappy apartment during her college years. Her Geist is a fibrous figure like insulation strands crossed with green mist and smoker's lung. His Keystone is a lens from an old camera. Known keys include Industrial and Phantasmal.<br /> <br /> A 'ghost photography' kind of ability would be cool for the pair, perhaps casting illusions into the scene as well. I'm not sure where to begin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T15:18:52-08:00","id":1016767,"title":"","content":"Hey there, I had an idea for a Mystic Art. I originally wanted to have it as a Legacy, but I'm having a hard time making it work like that. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1016266#post1016266\"><b>Here is the partial write up of the Legacy.</b></a> What do you think? How close did I get to capturing the essence of the Trickster archetype? What sorts of Attainments can you imagine for it as a Mystic Art?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-13-2016, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T18:48:02-08:00","id":1017431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1016767#post1016767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey there, I had an idea for a Mystic Art. I originally wanted to have it as a Legacy, but I'm having a hard time making it work like that.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1016266#post1016266\"><b>Here is the partial write up of the Legacy.</b></a> What do you think? How close did I get to capturing the essence of the Trickster archetype? What sorts of Attainments can you imagine for it as a Mystic Art?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrmmm, lets see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u><b>ANANSI BOYS</b></u><br /> <b>Resonant Path</b>: Mastigos<br /> <b>Primary Arcana</b>: Mind &amp; Prime<br /> <b>Yantra</b>: Symbols of mythological tricksters such as Coyote, Loki and Hermes (+1 or +2 if clearly visible), taboo-breaking fashion choices (+2), wisecracking (+1), mocking or destroying a representation of a scorned authority figure (+1 for a handheld representation or +2 for a detailed, life sized one), storytelling (+1 or +2), slight of hand (+1), disguises (+1 if basic or +2 if complex)<br /> <b>Oblations: </b>Pulling pranks, giving satirical performances, making oneself the comic relief, teaching unorthodox lessons<br /> <b>Attainments</b>:<ul><li><b>Deadpan </b>(\u2022\u2022): Spells cast by Tricksters with this attainment do not trigger the unseen senses of other Mages unless they also risk Paradox. (e.g. spells that don't exceed their reach don't draw attention).</li> <li><b>Pass The Buck</b> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): Tricksters are masters of deflection and disinformation, especially when it comes to shifting blame. A trickster with this attainment can bend the resonance of a spell to fit another mage. Said mage must be present, and the trickster must either have observed them casting a spell within the scene, or scrutinized a spell they've already cast. Once cast the spell will appear to scrutiny as though cast by the other sorcerer, not the trickster.</li> <li><b>All In Your Head</b> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): Tricksters gift for lying is not limited to the mundane, they excel at spinning the lie itself to their benefit. When casting a spell improved by a deceptive yantra (slight of hand, a disguise, an epic yarn, etc.) Sleepers only count as witnesses if they see through the deception associated with the spell. Those who fail are swept up in the magic and will write off even the most improbable events as perfectly normal. For instance, a Mage could lead several dozen people in a conga line across a pool, yet no one would ever wonder why they didn't fall in. Moreover, even if a sleeper is alerted to the wrongness of their situation, they add two dice to their Integrity roll to rationalize the events. This attainment does not influence unraveling, spells will still crumble after sleeper exposure.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>That's the best I got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T19:09:39-08:00","id":1017439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1017431#post1017431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the best I got.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like it! I think their Primary Yantra could be like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Masters Of Mischief:</b> The magic of the Anansi Boys works best when applied subtly and toward inflicting change and chaos (i.e. they benefit from an additional free Reach). As such, spells that are overt in nature or are meant to increase order or stability do not have affinity with this Art (i.e. they incur Paradox as though no Yantra had been used)..<br /> <br /> EDIT: Feel free to add this to your Google Doc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-14-2016, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T19:22:10-08:00","id":1017444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1017439#post1017439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like it! I think their Primary Yantra could be like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Masters Of Mischief:</b> The magic of the Anansi Boys works best when applied subtly and toward inflicting change and chaos (i.e. they benefit from an additional free Reach). As such, spells that are overt in nature or are meant to increase order or stability do not have affinity with this Art (i.e. they incur Paradox as though no Yantra had been used)..<br /> <br /> EDIT: Feel free to add this to your Google Doc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works. Though I think I'll phrase it: &quot;The magic of the Anansi Boys is intended to work subtly towards change and chaos. Spells that complicate existing problems or create new dilemmas benefit from an additional Free Reach, while those that resolve problems or create stability always invoke paradox.<br /> <br /> Though I'm considering dropping the free 'restrictive' attainment, as it's proven a bit of a headache to keep track of for characters with multiple arts.<br /> <br /> Regardless, added to the doc. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T20:05:04-08:00","id":1017925,"title":"","content":"Hey, PenDragon, have you ever thought of writing a Mystic Art for the Daksha?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T10:17:19-08:00","id":1018138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1017925#post1017925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, PenDragon, have you ever thought of writing a Mystic Art for the Daksha?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which book are they from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T13:04:00-08:00","id":1018194,"title":"","content":"Legacies: the Sublime. One of the most... unique Legacies, and one that I am fond of, and so is a player of mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T04:11:58-08:00","id":1024213,"title":"","content":"Sorry to ask for help finding something but I'm kinda stumped.<br /> <br /> What do the Primary Arcana of a Mystic Art do? The system section on pg.6 doesn't mention them, but the quick character build section says to take note of them.<br /> <br /> Are they just a vague indication of what the art primarily focuses on? Or is there something more significiant to them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T10:24:57-08:00","id":1024390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1024213#post1024213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to ask for help finding something but I'm kinda stumped.<br /> <br /> What do the Primary Arcana of a Mystic Art do? The system section on pg.6 doesn't mention them, but the quick character build section says to take note of them.<br /> <br /> Are they just a vague indication of what the art primarily focuses on? Or is there something more significiant to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>My original thought was to give Arts prereqs like Legacies, but I ended up dumping that in favor of greater character variety. I left in the Primary Arcana as a little guide to what Arcana the Arts favor. Though for certain Arts (like Tsuchimikado Onmyodo, which requires all spells use Spirit) the Primary Arcana really is a prereq.<br /> <br /> If I work up the chutzpah to do another pass of the doc I'll certainly clarify that, and probably change the 'Rotes' entry to 'Oblations'. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T23:43:07-07:00","id":1323875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=134083#post134083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, since there seems to be interest, I'll<br /> give a brief overview of my Promethean Hacks:<ul><li><b>Replace Humanity with Simulacre </b>(by Metamurpho, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9509-simulacre-an-alternative-morality-stat-for-prometheans\">here</a>): Simulacre defines how close a Promethean is to being human, and how human-like his body has become. At low Simulacre he's basically just an animate mass, no vital organs, no need to<br /> breath or eat, human in appearance only. As Simulacre rises those natural advantages<br /> begin to fade as more and more the Promethean<br /> acquires human needs, however, higher Simulacre also slows the growth of Wasteland and<br /> Disquite.</li> <li><b>Wasteland &amp; Disquiet: </b>Wasteland and Disquiet<br /> are intrinsically tied, one to the other. As a Promethean's wasteland grows so too does others' paranoia. Disquiet itself is no longer rolled for individuals, instead it<br /> is managed as a global track side-by-side with Wasteland. Both increment based on Simulacre, with low Simulacre incrementing in days, and high taking weeks, months or even years. However, certain events, like Transmutation usage, revealing of disfigurements and torment can cause immediate rolls.<ul><li>How individuals respond to Disquiet falls more on the shoulders of the Storyteller, no longer is it assumed every NPC will turn against them.<br /> Indeed, a mortal of sufficient Integrity can rough past Disquiet and see the Promethean for who he truly is. Conversely<br /> of course, low Integrity mortals have the opposite response, developing a profound and lasting obsession that endures even once the Promethean<br /> is gone.</li> <li><br /> Supernaturals are not affected in the same way as mortals, they feel disquiet<br /> certainly, but aren't <b>compelled </b>by it. Therefore it falls to that specific character to respond in a manner appropriate. That could mean that they can talk it out with the Prommie, but often other Supernaturals will mistake the feeling of unease for a sign that the Promethean is one of their natural enemies. A Werewolf may assume he's some<br /> sort of Host, a Changeling might mistake him for Fae, or a Sin-Eater could assume he's an immortal abomination. Ample room for both understanding and misunderstanding.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Bestowments: </b>All physical/mental bestowments<br /> are gone, instead a Promethean<br /> gets two attributes, one based on Lineage and the other on Refinement. Add one dot to each Attribute (which can take them over 5) and gain 9-again on all related rolls. Each Lineage has<br /> a number of advantages which take the place of other Bestowments, all lineages get 3, which<br /> are chosen during character creation (if<br /> unfleshed). These fade as Simulacre rises, losing the first at 4, the second at 7, and the last at 9.<ul><li><br /> Unfleshed are a lot more common.<br /> Indeed it would be better to say that all Prometheans are entirely unique. Building the specifics of your Promethean is a key portion of character creation, much<br /> like constructing a Demon's demonic form. Importantly, it is <b>not </b>the base assumption that Prommie's come from dead bodies. Golems, for instant, are generally made of clay and dirt.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Transmutations: </b>Remove the dot structure entirely, Transmutations<br /> are now purchased based on prerequisites. Like Jolt -&gt; Shock -&gt; Arc -&gt; Divine Lightning. Certain Transmutations have to be radically altered (Might being a big one) while others can go mostly untouched. Custom Transmutations<br /> are also strongly encouraged and everything gets an on-the-spot power up for GMC rules.<ul><li>Electroshock Recharge becomes inherent to all Prometheans, but automatically risks Torment when used.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Antagonists: </b>A new antagonist group, The Society of Thule, exists. Composed of mortal alchemists and mad scientists they seek to tame Pyros and bend it to their own interests. Their numbers include many Demiurges driven mad by the generative act<br /> as well as though whose experience with Disquiet left them permanently deranged. The abilities of the Society and Demiurges<br /> are strongly inspired by the fan game Genius: The Transgression, albeit significantly toned down.</li> </ul><br /> That's the gist, there's a bunch of other small changes<br /> as well, but those are the big ones.<br /> <br /> P.S. I've got a fair number of Geist hacks<br /> as well, for those interested.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been on<br /> a bit of a Promethean fixation lately, so I've got to ask. How are these changed for 2e?.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12398,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","user":"DArchon5","date":". 07-12-2019, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T14:18:41-07:00","id":1325063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1323875#post1323875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been on<br /> a bit of a Promethean fixation lately, so I've got to ask. How are these changed for 2e?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh hey, I haven't seen a post here in a while.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I haven't touched CofD in a few years, and Promethean in longer. TBH I hate Promethean 2e, it doubled down on all my least favorite parts of 1e and implemented a power system so complex I began looking at Exalted charm trees fondly. It was so bloated I didn't even know how to begin to homebrew for it, so I didn't.<br /> <br /> Sorry if that's not what you wanted to hear. That said, if I ever run CofD again I'll likely repurpose Deviant for Prommies. Everything I've read about that game indicates it'll be a weird, modular setting that can be bent to mimic different splats and already caters to many Promethean style stories.<br /> <br /> Also, while I'm at it, a shameless plug. I'm Storytelling Scion nowdays and streaming the games most Sunday on Twitch. The game is the Demi-Dozen and I'm told its pretty funny: <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/scabbyrooster/videos\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.twitch.tv/scabbyrooster/videos</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T20:00:50-07:00","id":1325132,"title":"","content":"How the fuck are Transmutations complex?<br /> <br /> And Christ then, what <i>was</i> your favorite parts of 1e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T09:31:09-07:00","id":1325275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1325132#post1325132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Christ then, what <i>was</i> your favorite parts of 1e?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the general concept of playing an outsider being trying to make sense of life and humanity, but the setting, crunch and feel of the game are not for me. I don't enjoy running it, my players don't want to play it. In fairness the Promethean characters in the mixed games I ran went over well, they made interesting foils to the action, but I found myself dumping most of the crunch in order to make them mesh. I've accepted that Promethean isn't a game meant for me.<br /> <br /> As I said above, I've drifted away from CofD as a whole. I've been tinkering with Storypath and find it more to my liking.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T19:29:02-07:00","id":1325463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1325275#post1325275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the general concept of playing an outsider being trying to make sense of life and humanity, but the setting, crunch and feel of the game are not for me. I don't enjoy running it, my players don't want to play it. In fairness the Promethean characters in the mixed games I ran went over well, they made interesting foils to the action, but I found myself dumping most of the crunch in order to make them mesh. I've accepted that Promethean isn't a game meant for me.<br /> <br /> As I said above, I've drifted away from CofD as a whole. I've been tinkering with Storypath and find it more to my liking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand this sentiment.<br /> <br /> But okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T23:26:37-07:00","id":1325504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1325463#post1325463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand this sentiment.<br /> <br /> But okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>People like and dislike different things. Sorry \u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T16:19:26-07:00","id":1478980,"title":"","content":"Do you have any plans for adding more material to your Proximi House Rules? I wanna use them someday. I noticed you said your Proximi Dynasties draw their 3 Arcana from specific Legacies, but the Sons Of Bezalel and House Telyavel have sets of Arcana that don't match any canon Paths, and canon Legacies are usually based on the Ruling Arcana of a Path, plus a Third Ruling Arcanum. Therefore, shouldn't the Sons Of Bezalel be based on some sort of Moros + Mind Legacy, and House Telyavel be based on some sort of Thyrsus + Death Legacy? Could I just remove the part where it says Proximi Dynasties are linked to specific Legacies, without causing mechanical or narrative issues? Could a Proximus Dynasty have more than one signature Skill? It seems House Telyavel could have Medicine or Occult or Survival, for example. And what's the rationale behind the rule which says Yantras used by Proximi only give +1 regardless of type? Seems like arbitrary nerfing. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-16-2022, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-28T16:19:33-07:00","id":1479670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1478980#post1478980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have any plans for adding more material to your Proximi House Rules? I wanna use them someday. I noticed you said your Proximi Dynasties draw their 3 Arcana from specific Legacies, but the Sons Of Bezalel and House Telyavel have sets of Arcana that don't match any canon Paths, and canon Legacies are usually based on the Ruling Arcana of a Path, plus a Third Ruling Arcanum. Therefore, shouldn't the Sons Of Bezalel be based on some sort of Moros + Mind Legacy, and House Telyavel be based on some sort of Thyrsus + Death Legacy? Could I just remove the part where it says Proximi Dynasties are linked to specific Legacies, without causing mechanical or narrative issues? Could a Proximus Dynasty have more than one signature Skill? It seems House Telyavel could have Medicine or Occult or Survival, for example. And what's the rationale behind the rule which says Yantras used by Proximi only give +1 regardless of type? Seems like arbitrary nerfing. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a></div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest I don't. It's been a while since I ran CoD, or any OP games for that matter (save for an entirely homebrewed Exalted).<br /> <br /> As for my rational while writing the Proximi, I was designing them largely as a stand alone thing and didn't want to lock my concepts to the 5 canon paths. And the Yantra thing was purely for ease of book keeping. That said, I would encourage you to make any changes you desire for your own table. That's the spirit of homebrew after all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T11:07:24-07:00","id":1485997,"title":"","content":"Somehow I totally failed to post my now half-decade old 2e adaptation for my Proximi rules. It's not 100% complete, but since a few people have shown interest, here it is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15nDWq-hcLZa-1aJzEtnuf4pxmDE6nn7JpHEaw7wLuhI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> 